#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot sets your blade beside his tools. \"Come back in two hours. I will see to the edge and the worn metal.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot checks the blade. \"Still in good condition. No repair needed yet. Keep your materials.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"The blade needs work. Bring one steel lump and 50 charcoal, and leave it with me for two hours.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Leave this blade, one steel lump and 50 charcoal with Godot? The repair takes two hours."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Show Godot a blade"
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot lays your repaired blade at your feet. \"Good as new. Take it.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"Your blade is not beside my tools. If you took it, bring the same blade back so I can finish.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"Not yet. Give me two hours from when you left the blade.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"Leave it here this time. Another two hours; you have already paid for the materials.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Return your blade to Godot"
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Close this repair order? The materials have been used and will not be returned. No blade will be replaced."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "You left a blade with me. I need two hours at the forge. If you took it away, bring the same blade back."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Show me the blade first. No sense working sound metal. If it needs repair, leave it with one steel lump and 50 charcoal. Come back in two hours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have a look at my blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is my blade ready?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I took the blade. Here it is again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Close the repair order."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "About my blade repair."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot: blade repair."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "*Blade repair. The agreed time has passed. Return to Godot at the forge to collect your blade."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "*Blade repair. Godot has the blade and the materials. Allow two hours, then return to the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Homemade early battle sword
msgid "Homemade Guts' battle sword"
msgstr ""

#. Homemade early battle sword
msgid "A roughly forged copy of Guts' broad battle sword. The uneven edge still bites deep, but the heavy blade pulls against the hand and its imperfect temper makes it prone to damage."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still alive, I see! Is your sword in one piece?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It has been a while. Heard what is happening? Even the daylight seems darker. Something bad has happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Back again. What is it this time?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You left a blade here. Have you come about the repair?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still waiting for the steel and the rest of your delivery."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your blade is at the forge. Ask me how the work is going."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your great blade has not been forgotten. What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Awake at last. Last time you crossed the threshold on your own feet. This time someone had to carry you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Easy. You have been through enough. This is my forge. I am Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot looks at your blade, then raises his eyes. \"Guts. Thought I would recognize you by that iron when I could no longer make out your face. What is it? Straighten your sword again?\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you want a forge, you have found it. Mind what you touch. I am not fond of strangers. Rickert can show you where to rest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*The smith turns the billet in his tongs. Only after a few hammer blows does he notice you. \"Close the door. And step away from that bucket.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Griffith... Where is that bastard?!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where is everyone?! What was that dream?!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where is my hand? Where is Rickert? What the hell happened?!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where is Rickert? What happened?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Who brought me here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How long have I been here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My belongings..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know how I can repay you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you Godot? I am looking for a smith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I heard you can mend weapons here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I was looking for somewhere to rest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It still serves me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a better blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good to see you, old man."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is work to discuss."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Just looking in."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us talk, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What sort of work do you take?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a good sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You found him. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Blades, iron, fittings. Show me the thing and I will tell you whether it is worth the work. Gears and little mechanisms are Rickert's business. His eyes are better than mine."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is my blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rumors do not do my work for me. Show me. Put it on the edge of the table, away from the heat."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Understood. Thank you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is a place for a traveler. Rickert can show you. No sleeping in the workshop, and leave the tools alone."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Then we have an understanding."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see. A more careful owner would make it last longer. Put it here; let me look."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me the old one first. What remains of it tells me more than your wishes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then stop standing in the doorway. You are letting in a draft."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not lie to me. Let me have a look."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Bed upstairs. You know the rest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Calm down or you will pass out again. You have no strength left."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Easy. Rest first; we can talk when you have recovered. You can tell me what happened then."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Long enough. I do not count the hours at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First make sure you can stand. Then count your iron."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You were lying in my arms, barely breathing. What else was I to do? Not the gift I would have chosen, but here we are."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Get back on your feet first. I do not bargain with a dying man over water and a place by the wall."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot tell you what you saw. I only know the wounds are real."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A knight. Tall, armored. He laid you down here and told us to prepare water. Ask him the rest; he is waiting outside."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "An armored knight brought you. Said you could recover here. He has gone on his way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your body is no excuse for what you do with your hands. Speak, and keep your quarrels away from the boy and my hearth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Speak, Guts. The iron is cooling."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What did you want to ask?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About my order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How long have you lived at the forge?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted to ask about Rickert."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is something I need to tell you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something is changing in me. I accepted it to survive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what is happening to me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will stay here a while."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will go and find the materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back if you have work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Until next time, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Stay. Just leave the passage clear; do not stand in the way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Go on. Check the list before you leave so you do not have to make the trip twice."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back and we will see what is ready by then."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me the iron and tell me what it must endure."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a reliable heavy sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a sword for fighting those creatures."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have a look at this sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have a look at this homemade copy."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I made this blade myself. What do you think?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My blade needs inspection."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "They say you once made a sword to kill a dragon."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About an order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why use different steels in a sword?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I brought ore. Will that do?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About making a new blade for me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot taps the anvil without turning. \"Another soldier full of stories. A sword is a tool. It must be balanced and quick. Too heavy, and you will die winding up for the first swing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right, forget it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a powerful blade. It need not be that extreme."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can handle the weight. Ordinary swords break when I put all my strength into them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back if you need something. Ask Rickert, too. He may have something useful for you. Not a sword, but useful all the same."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you take the work?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There. You can listen after all. I can try, but you will have to bring the materials. I am too old to go looking for them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Listen. A sword is forged for a person. It must be an extension of the hand. I have done this since I could hold tongs. I will not waste steel and heat on a useless monstrosity no one can fight with."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then make a blade I can use."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Think. No need to hurry before the iron is in the fire."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Put it down. Even that much iron has parts that need watching."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me see. Has the grip turned? Does the guard press into your palm? How is the swing?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Heavy. Familiar to you, then. The edge shows it has not been idle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It serves me well."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It needs repair."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you improve it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I thought it was almost impossible to break."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It feels different now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then the fitting was worth the work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not without changing its shape and finding the balance all over again. That would mean making a new sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Anything can break. Especially if you keep testing whether it can take one more blow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me the grip. Then take it again. We will see whether it is the blade or you getting used to it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then keep looking after it. A sound blade deserves that much."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot turns the sword, checks the grip and draws a thumb across the edge. \"Someone took pains with this. Still a long way from a fine blade, but better than nothing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot checks the grip and the edge. \"What matters is how it behaves in the hand. You worked at it, I can see. A long way from a fine blade, but better than nothing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You could have praised it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There was no other suitable weapon."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted to learn."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Flattery makes a worse smith. Your life depends on the blade; one mistake can end it. Do not take offense."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A good reason to pick up a hammer. Live with it now. You will feel where you went wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep it, then. Pick it up again after a few more attempts and you will see the mistakes for yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Hmph. I did. A long time ago."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do dragons even exist?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why take such an order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Who could use it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you consider that sword a failure?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The puffed-up fool who sent the plans never thought about that. He wanted a toy everyone would talk about. Vanity brings plenty of foolish things into the world."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "An order from above. They asked for a sword that could cut a dragon, so I forged one. I met the terms exactly. Nobody thought to ask whether an ordinary man could lift it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "None of those pampered lords could use it. That was then. You know what sort of hands it has reached now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Nobody then. Certainly none of the pampered lords who ordered it. Not a knight in the kingdom could use it. It stayed there, dead weight."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The iron was what I intended: strong and deadly. But it was useless to the people it was meant for. A smith must think about the hands that will carry his work. You have reminded me of that."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. The iron was exactly what I meant it to be: strong and deadly. It was useless to the people it was meant for. A smith must think about the hands that will carry his work. That blade waits for someone as mad as it is."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The same creatures that left those wounds on you?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A blade for fighting those creatures? Tell me why you need it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ordinary weapons shatter against them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want to reach whoever is behind this nightmare."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need to protect myself and those I care about."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you make me a Dragonslayer?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Creatures of the abyss are no wild beasts. If ordinary steel will not do, we must make a blade that bears the impact without dragging its owner into the grave."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before the one at the top, there are those below. You order it with rage in your eyes, but you must carry it on the days when you have no strength left to be angry."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Protection is a heavier burden than revenge. Then listen. Where will you fight? How much can you carry? What balance are you used to? I need honest answers."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I know a blade that could hew demons. That old design. I also know how much good steel and charcoal it takes. We will not finish it in an evening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what to bring. I will find it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need time to prepare."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Soft steel folds at the edge; brittle steel breaks. Heat, temper and shape must suit the work. Bring sound steel, not a promise of it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ore has to be smelted first. For these orders, bring steel ready for the forge. Rickert can help you tell the pieces apart."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Try stores of metal, old workshops, or steel you have smelted yourself. Keep the good high-carbon pieces separate from the ordinary steel."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will return what you brought for the unfinished blade. The work is over."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we go on, tell me what has been troubling you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is needed, what you brought, and what is left to do. That is a proper order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The battle sword order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The Dragonslayer order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the blade repair."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I lost my road journal. I need another."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something has been weighing on you. If it concerns this work, tell me before we continue."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My answer has not changed. There will be no new blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A long battle sword, no ornaments. Bring 4 steel lumps, 1 high-steel lump, 200 charcoal and 2 leather patches, all together. Then give me twelve hours at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For this delivery: 4 steel lumps, 1 high-steel lump, 200 charcoal and 2 leather patches. Bring the whole lot so I can begin."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "In the forge. Metal does not like haste. You can see to your own equipment while I work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Finished. Come over here and take it by the grip."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "That order is settled. We have nothing more to exchange for it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You already have the blade. If you left materials for another, take them back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The materials are here. Everything you asked for."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will take the finished blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do I still need to bring?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why so long? I am short of time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I already have the blade. Return the unused materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have changed. What about our agreement?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You promised to return the materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Inspect my blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Because I will not give you a weapon with a hidden crack I could have found in the forge. Heat, hammering and cooling take their time. Want quick? Find a club in the woods. Want to live? Wait."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. The metal is here. Now it is my work. Give me twelve hours and do not hover over my shoulder."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. That part is settled. Ask what is needed next before you leave."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is needed now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will return everything you brought. I have no use for what is not mine. Come here and take it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need to explain what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First I need 32 steel lumps, in loads of eight. Then 8 high-steel lumps, 600 charcoal and 4 leather patches. After the final delivery, give me two days."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need 32 steel lumps in all. You have brought <u_val:berserk_godo_sword_iron_given>. Bring another load of eight when you can."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The ordinary steel is here. Now bring 8 high-steel lumps, 600 charcoal and 4 leather patches."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are eight steel lumps."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are the high steel, charcoal and leather."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. The metal is here. Now it is my work. Give me two days and do not hover over my shoulder."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have settled the account. There will be no blade for this order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Finished. Take the grip. Now lift it... Careful! Do not swing; I still need that ceiling. How does it feel?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It sits well in the hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Heavier than I expected..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Remember that feeling. If the grip starts to shift, repair it before it loosens completely."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Learn its weight in an open space, not a narrow passage full of creatures. Bring the blade back into guard after each blow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot clears a space beside the enormous black blade. \"Finished. Come around and help me shift it. A blade for things a man was never meant to fight. Your Dragonslayer.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "With this, I will finally have a chance."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will come back, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A chance, yes. It is only iron. The rest, whether you live or die, is yours to do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back. We will see how this iron serves against your demons."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep your grip. And... take care of yourself, boy."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You left me a blade. Two hours at the forge; then come and ask for it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Put it in the light. First I will inspect it. If it is sound, keep your steel. If it needs work, I need the blade, one steel lump, 50 charcoal and two hours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the Dragonslayer..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The coals will keep. Ask."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why live so far from other people?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How long have you worked at the anvil?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are old and ill. You could have put the hammer down long ago."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me sit by your forge a while."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember what you told me at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here I can hear my own hammer. In town, people sometimes cannot hear their own work through all the empty talk."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do people bother you that much?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "But customers must be harder to find here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you and Rickert get lonely here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Since I could hold tongs. First I carried billets and water and worked the bellows. Then I was graciously allowed to spoil the iron myself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you spoil much good iron?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When did you know you were a master?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I could have. Long ago."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then why keep going?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Every morning I see what I did not finish the night before. I know where my day begins. By noon a shapeless lump has become a thing someone can use. Enough to feel alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you never want a different life?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you understand, you have been luckier than most wanderers."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A man who knows why he came does not bother me. Being asked to admire a crest for half a day instead of making a sound weapon does."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have more than enough work. Extra gold will not make these hands younger."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert always finds a way to break the silence. Sometimes before I have had time to miss it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Enough. Some of the rubbish I made when I was young still makes me ashamed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When I stopped blaming the steel every time a blade cracked. Steel does not lie. The smith's hand does."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted plenty of things when I was young and foolish. But I always came back to this forge of my own accord."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He has learned a few things. Invented a few more while I grumbled about making simple things complicated."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What sort of things?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you approve of his inventions?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why did you let him stay here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert is taking our conversation hard."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert decided to leave the forge and travel with me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Talk to Rickert. Tell him to come with me. He will listen to you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Fastenings, triggers, little springs. I would make a thicker piece of solid steel. He spends an hour on a drawing, removes half the iron, and the damned thing still works."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If it survives a real fight, yes. If it breaks in the hand, he makes it again. Better for his hands than any praise."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The boy needed a place to live. He has lost his companions. There was room here, and another piece of bread."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The boy needed somewhere to live. There was room here and another piece of bread."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is that the only reason?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you want a longer, tearful story? If you can help the boy, you help. No need to make a speech."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see it. His hammer falls out of rhythm; he overheats the forge. It is hard on him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He has more questions than answers. Do not make him guess what you are able to tell him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I did not know how to tell him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have not been able to tell him everything."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How should I speak to him now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Nobody knows the right words for that. Losing people is a blow to the head, however you dress it up."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not promise some vague later if you cannot do it now. Tell him plainly: I will tell you the rest when I can. He can understand honesty."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not expect him to understand it all and move on today. Give him time. When he can speak, let him ask his questions. Answer without hiding behind excuses."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He decided that himself? Without you leaning on him?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. It was his decision."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Remember that he has a head of his own. A companion, not spare hands for your weapon or a slave to carry loot. Treat him with respect."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I understand, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not want to let him go, do you?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Do not make me search the woods for you if a hair on his head is harmed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not. I am old and used to having the boy here. But I will not lock him inside for my own comfort. His road is his to choose."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He has given his answer. Do not go around him through me. He has his own life. If he said no, respect it. Go about your business and stop begging."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Set the iron down. I am listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My companions died in that nightmare."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "People were dying in that nightmare. I still remember it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will find him. Whatever it costs."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something is changing in me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sit by the fire. We can talk."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I should have done something. Saved them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still remember their voices."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot go on talking about this now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What could you have done against that abyss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I should have died with them!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I need to be alone."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then do not pretend you knew the answer and chose cowardice. You did what a human body could do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "But you are alive. By a miracle or by your teeth, you got out. Now you have to live with that. Living on is the hard part."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you cannot, you cannot. No need to tear the wound open. We can sit quietly by the forge. Warm yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us sit quietly."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about one of them, if you want. Who they were before that day. Remember people alive, not torn apart."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Judeau."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Pippin."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Corkus."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not yet. Thank you for listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He looked after the people beside him. Tell me about that, not just the way he died."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you. Enough for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A man who stood between danger and his companions. That is worth remembering."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A man has more to him than a sharp tongue. What did he hope for?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A life beyond battle. Work, a place of his own. Not a foolish dream."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I believe you. If you have the strength, you will find him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is that all? You will not try to stop me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What would be the point? You did not come for my blessing. But revenge is the end of a road. When you want to talk about how to reach that day without losing your mind, I will be here at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can see what is happening to you. Your skin, your eyes... Why did you let that corruption in?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What change? Explain it properly."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I was given this power. My body is becoming something else."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I took the power from one of those creatures."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I agreed to serve those who are stronger. This is the price."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You promised to return the battle sword materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You promised to return the Dragonslayer materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I already have the sword. Will you demand it back?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "May I remain at the forge?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you understand where it will end? Iron changes in the forge too. Leave it too long and it becomes slag."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I needed the power to survive!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still decide what I do. My mind is my own."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not want to argue, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Defeating it was not enough? You chose to become it. The abyss can poison people even after its creatures die."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Serve them? What if your master tells you to turn that weapon on the people you came to for help?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Maybe you did. Everyone wants to live. But I will not forge a sword for this new road of yours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You agreed to help me before. Why refuse now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then listen to my answer while you can. I will not make that blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then we will not argue. I have told you the work I will not take."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You came as a person asking for a person's weapon. Now you ask me to arm what you are becoming. I do not know that creature. I will not help it grow stronger."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you throwing me out?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is that your final answer?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I refused to forge you a blade. The rest depends on your behavior under my roof. Act like a person and you may remain."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Final."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is yours. You fought with it; you answer for it. I will not tear it out of your hands. But if the Dragonslayer breaks, I will not take new work on it for this road."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "In a hurry? Stay a little. Hand me those long tongs."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Let me help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sorry, old man. Another time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "As you wish. Go about your business."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot lifts the white-hot billet from the forge. Light crosses his worn face. The hammer falls; sparks scatter across the dark earthen floor. \"What do you see before you?\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot returns to the iron. He does not resume the conversation."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Iron. Fire. Sparks."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see your work, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Nothing special. Let us talk about something else."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I watched those sparks when I was a child. Thought that beauty was worth swinging a hammer all day. Fool that I was."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What changed?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "They let me hold the billet myself. Soon learned to watch my fingers and where I was striking, not the sparks."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is left after the fire?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then look closer. The finest-looking thing here disappears the quickest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The sparks go out. The iron remains."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A bright spark, then nothing. But the iron remains. Each morning I can see what I did yesterday. Where I straightened it. Where I ruined the steel."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "People are more complicated than iron."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you saying I only look at the sparks?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is what remains after the fire really enough for you?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course. Iron is more honest. It does not try to tell me that a crack inside has done it good."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you see in me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you talking about my anger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you think remains for me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have changed. Does it still apply to me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have not accused you of anything. I asked what you could see in the dark."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not every day. But I can return to the anvil next morning and go on with the work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have lived from one battle to the next a long time. You know where to stand, where to strike, and how to reach the next dawn."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is what I do best."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see that. But what will you do with a peaceful day? One day without a fight?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will find something worth living for."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know. I never thought about it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will decide when that day comes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your anger got you out of the grave. But even here by the fire you sit as though you must spring up and run."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "While I sit here warming myself, he is out there. Alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Perhaps. And you? Are you alive?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "As long as I can hold a weapon and fight."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If I stop for a moment, it will all come back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not understand. You were not there."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You ask whether your blade can survive the next creature. Suppose it can. What will you do when the fighting is over?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You ask whether your blade will last another fight. Suppose it does. What will you do with a day when you do not have to swing it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want a safe place where I can just live."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There are people I need to return to."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now I just want to survive tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You chose to change your nature for strength. What will you hold on to with that changed body?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My own life. I want to protect it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can protect the people I care about with this strength."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Freedom. Nobody will dare command me now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Search hard, boy. Do not expect a purpose to appear as if by magic when you kill your last enemy."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is no shame in not knowing. At least you can begin with that admission."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Mind that the habit of killing does not decide for you before you can open your mouth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "And when your wounded body cannot raise the blade? Will you deny yourself the right to live that day? A sword cannot replace a beating heart."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Fear is a poor companion. If the nightmares return, there is someone here who can sit beside you until they quiet down. You are not alone in these woods."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. I was not in your hell. But I can see what is happening here. I can see how carelessly you treat the little you managed to keep."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A good aim. Keep it in mind. One day you must decide what to do with your hands besides striking."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then make the journey. Try to get back before they tire of waiting or die. The road takes more time than you think."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Fair enough. Find a few minutes even in the worst day that you do not have to give wholly to fear."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Everyone wants to live. Then do not hurry to throw away everything human you had before this choice."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let them speak to you as equals. Even when they say things your new nature does not like. Do not become their monster."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Pride. Then you must answer for each step yourself. That takes more strength than empty threats."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot turns back to the anvil. \"Enough talk. The iron is cooling.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me work the bellows."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for the conversation, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I should go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Steadily. Not too hard yet; do not burn through the coal."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Mm."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Give me back the tongs and do not get in the way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "And what have you decided?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still thinking. It is not simple."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I think I have something to return to."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am not hurrying you. These things take time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Then we did not sit here for nothing."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "At Godot's hearth"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ask what you came to ask."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts. Still alive. Sit down and catch your breath."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My body is changing. Can we talk about a new blade?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will not take new work on the Dragonslayer. I can still inspect an ordinary blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we discuss this blade, tell me what has been weighing on you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I accepted an inhuman power. What about my sword?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. The iron was what I intended: strong and deadly. It was useless to the people it was meant for. A smith must think about the hands that will carry his work. A blade like that only makes sense for someone as mad as the design."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Hey. Can you hear me? It is Rickert. Take it slowly. You are back at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are at the woodland forge. Godot lives here; he is a smith, and I help him. I am Rickert."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are awake. Good. I am Rickert. We tended your wounds when you were brought here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You frightened me. Really. Next time, try opening your eyes a little sooner. I had time to imagine the worst."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts?.. Guts, you are awake!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have not forgotten your bolts. Have you come about the batch?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still waiting for the metal for your hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The first delivery is here. I still need the small fittings."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your mechanism is being looked after. Shall we discuss the work?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts! I heard steps and thought Godot was sending me for charcoal again. Have you been here long?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Oh, you are alive! How was the road? Legs intact, equipment holding up?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Shall we stop for a moment, or talk as we walk?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Careful, do not step there. A pin the size of a fingernail. I have lost it in the grass twice already... Ah. Sorry. Are you here for Godot?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Hello. I am Rickert; I help at the forge. What brings you here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts. Good to see you on your feet. What did you want to talk about?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will listen. Just give me a little room while we talk."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I need a smith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First I wanted to see what you are making."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am looking for somewhere to sleep."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wait. Who brought me here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert... Thank you for helping."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Give me some time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have been here before."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember Godot, but we have not spoken."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is it safe here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me what you are working on."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need help with equipment."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what happened..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the place I came back from."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would like to know more about you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About our road."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About your decision not to travel with me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something is happening to me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You were not there when I came back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He is at the forge. Wait until he puts down the hammer; otherwise he will not hear a thing. I am Rickert. I help him here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does he always greet people like that?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have not even spoken to him yet! Sometimes he barks so loudly you want to turn around. Then he takes work every other smith would refuse."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Checking the trigger. Sometimes it releases a moment late. On a table you barely notice; with the string drawn, that little fault can cost a life."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you notice the fault yourself?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Trying to make it stronger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. At first I thought I had assembled it badly. Took it apart, put it back together: same problem. Now I am looking for the part wearing faster than the others."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now, I would settle for it firing when I pull the trigger instead of when it feels like it. The rest can wait."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is room upstairs. Tell Godot before staying, though, or he may mistake you for something worse than a traveler. Leave the tools where they are; if you need something, ask."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you live here too?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I work. Learn. Occasionally even sleep, when Godot cannot find another urgent job."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A knight in a skull-shaped helm. He brought you here, then went on his way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A knight in a skull-shaped helm. He brought you to the door. We were too busy tending your wounds to ask him much."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am glad you woke up. Really glad."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I am nearby if you need me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then you know the place. We only get to meet now. Not the best circumstances, but here we are."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He said he had seen you before. I mostly help with the work here. I will try to help you, too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now, yes. It is quiet outside. We are nearby. We can talk about the rest when you feel better."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You needed help. We could give it. Do we need a better reason?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You came back... What happened to you? I was not there; I did not see. Tell me when you can. It does not have to be now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "With a crossbow I can help before the enemy reaches us. I am no swordsman. I choose a position early and try not to waste a shot; there may not be another."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What if you miss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could it reload faster?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you rather learn the sword?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where do you get your ideas?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "This world has things you have never seen."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still working on that trigger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then I will be glad I chose cover before firing. Looking for it with a blade at your throat is a little late."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The mechanism can change. Convenience costs weight, complexity or reliability. Make it lighter, and rain may trouble it; faster, and it may jam. I have more testing to do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would like to. But I will not become stronger than everyone who attacks me. Better to do what I know well than do badly what others live for."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Usually something starts annoying me. A strap rubs, a fastening takes too long to open, a part cannot be replaced on the road. Then I cannot stop thinking until I find a way to fix it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does it always work?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does Godot help?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course not. Sometimes fixing one problem creates a worse one. That is why I test things here, again and again. Better I break it safely than someone breaks it in battle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "In his own way. I know more about mechanisms; he sees through the metal. I spend half a day on a clever drawing, he looks once and says, \"It will break here.\" He is almost always right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have you brought something? Show me before I try to guess how it works."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here, take a look."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have seen those things before. What do you think?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sometimes I can tell what a thing does from its shape. But how they made it so small and even... I would spend a week fitting one part by hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you reproduce it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you interested?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Some parts, perhaps. The rest I would have to learn from nothing, and I am not sure our forge has the tools. I will not promise to build an unfamiliar thing after looking once."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Very. Just bring things that are unloaded and cannot go off by themselves. I have to examine them with my hands."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Godot handles blades. I can make bolts; ask me about what you need."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Can you do something about my hand?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where can I rest?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is working with Godot like?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Which work did you want to discuss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the prosthesis."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you still finish my order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I promised to finish the work, and I keep my word. That does not change my decision about traveling with you. Work is one thing; the road is another."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Godot grumbles, but he lets me try. When I ruin something, he makes me explain what I did wrong. Sometimes that is harder than doing it over."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We can talk about the crossbow or another job."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How is the mounting? Does it press or chafe?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have not fitted it yet? I can show you again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "That order is settled. If there is a problem with the device, tell me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us go over what is still needed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I think so. First I need to work out a mounting that holds without pressing on the wound. Then a mechanical hand. A small barrel can fit inside."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You want to put a cannon in it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First I just need to hold things again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will it survive a shot?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What will you need?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the mounting."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the arm cannon."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Remind me how to fit it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I assembled this mechanism myself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I came across this device."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you still help with my hand while my body changes?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am not ready for this yet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. One shot, then it must be loaded again by hand. There is little space. But at arm's length one shot may be enough to keep you alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The mounting and grip come first. If it cannot be worn all day without rubbing or falling apart, a barrel will be no use."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It needs good metal and careful fitting. I will test it before handing it over. But a charge is a charge; you still have to be careful."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Come back to it when you decide. I will not hurry you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Godot can help with the metal, but I will assemble and fit the mechanism. He thinks in blades and armor. This is smaller, finer work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you sure you can do it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I trust you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am sure I will give it all the care I can. If it does not work, I will remake it as often as I must. You have to live with this hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You already have a mechanism. We should look after that one."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First, 8 lumps of steel and 2 pipes. After that, 2 springs, 4 leather patches and 200 charcoal. I will need six hours after the last delivery."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Right now I need 8 lumps of steel and 2 pipes. Bring them together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The steel and pipes are here. Next I need 2 springs, 4 leather patches and 200 charcoal. Do not bring the first delivery again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Finished. Let me show you the mounting first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not finished yet. The materials are here; do not worry. Go about your business for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have settled this order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us make it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are the steel and pipes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are the springs, leather and charcoal."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Collect the finished device."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I already have a device. Return the materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would Godot be better suited to this?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is the hardest part?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Can you do this on the road?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will look for what you need."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not need a replacement hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Now everything is here. Give me six hours to assemble and test it properly."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes, this will do. I can work on the base. Bring the smaller fittings when you can."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Getting the parts out of one another's way. On a quiet table everything moves easily. Add straps, load, grit and sweat, and a generous gap is suddenly too small."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We need the forge for the heavy parts. If we travel together, we will return here to hand over the materials and collect the mechanism."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is what you brought. Keep the device you already have."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is where it holds to the arm. The load goes here, not on the stump. Fit it without a charge first. If it presses or moves, do not simply tighten it harder."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How do I put it on?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What about the cannon?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you, Rickert."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Take the device and start with the main mounting. You can fasten it yourself. I will show you the order of the straps so nothing twists."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Get used to the hand first. Loading and using the barrel take separate practice. Before doing anything with it, check where that barrel is pointing."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are welcome. It may feel strange or unpleasant at first. Give yourself time; a body does not get used to it at once."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still feels strange."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It holds well."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want to check the device."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Start small: pick up something light, put it down, repeat. Let yourself get used to the weight before testing it in battle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Still check the straps after a long road. Dust, water and strain will tell in time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course. The mounting, or the mechanism itself?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How should I care for it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why only one shot?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you make another?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep the moving parts clean of grit and fouling. Check the mounting after every shot. If something moves differently, find out why before firing again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is little room and weight to spare. Another loading mechanism would take space the hand needs to grip. I chose the hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You already have one to use. If something is wrong with it, let us look at that rather than make a second for storage."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep grit out of the joint and watch the straps. At the forge I can repair a damaged loose mechanism: one steel lump and 50 charcoal."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show the damaged mechanism."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wait... You assembled this without the hand? Fitting those small parts with one hand is no small task. I am impressed. I would have sworn at every step."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You understand mechanisms. Sound work. How does it behave under load?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I had to adapt."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not on the first try."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you show me how? It could help someone else in the same position."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I believe it. Some parts are hard enough with two hands. The result matters more than how many tries it took."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me see. First we should check whether the mounting fits you. A device made for another arm can rub you raw in an hour."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can try. I need to see how your body is changing. If the mounting stops fitting, do not force it; it could hurt you more than help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you afraid of me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still need help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am worried. I do not know how this ends, for you or the people around you. But you are standing here asking for help. For now that is enough for me to listen."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What did you want to know about the mechanism?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is precise metalwork. You need a forge, suitable tools and a good understanding of mechanisms. If you would rather bring materials, I can assemble it here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your ten bolts are finished. Come for them at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am working on the batch. Half an hour from the delivery; the materials are already here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I make wooden bodkin bolts with steel tips. For ten: 1 steel chunk, 1 stick, 20 thread, 10 feathers and 50 charcoal. Half an hour at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Make a batch."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is everything you need."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Collect the finished bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What types can you make?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Agreed. Bring the materials and I will get to it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good, hand them over. I will check the dimensions and quality."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are your bolts. Check how they sit in the groove before setting out; better to find a bad fit now than in battle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wooden shafts and pointed steel tips. The point helps, but the bow and the shot still matter."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What would you like to know? What I remember most are little things: who sat where by the fire, who always lost something and searched for it in the dark."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What were they like away from battle?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you fight with them?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What was Griffith like?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Judeau, Pippin, Corkus and Gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you miss the camp?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what happened to the Band."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Different people. Hearing us argue, laugh and share the last bread by the fire, you would never guess we would fight shoulder to shoulder the next morning."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I did what I could. Not everyone can cut through a battle the way you can, but there was work for all of us."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Not everyone could fight like Guts, but there was work for all of us, even me with a crossbow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I thought I knew the answer. I thought I was following someone who led us toward something real."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I believed in him. You say the Band is gone, but I still do not know what became of him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Beside him it felt like we were going somewhere, not just surviving another battle. That is why people followed. Why I followed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you think of him now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Now I do not know what to say. Perhaps the person he was with me was real too. Perhaps not. I do not want to guess which parts deserved my faith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Some things, yes. Others, not a bit."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For example?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not miss the wet blanket. Or everyone remembering broken equipment a minute before marching, as if they had planned it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You still do that here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you miss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here I can at least say \"wait\" without chasing the marching Band with my tools."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The people. Even when they would not let me work in peace. It is quiet now. Too quiet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you actually know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Not all at once, though. A piece at a time, or I start drowning in it again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have you learned anything about the people who attacked the camp, or where they took Griffith?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts... Where are they? What happened to everyone?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You were there. Will you tell me what you saw?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The Band was lost."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I saw what happened. Griffith gave people to those creatures."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Griffith offered them as a sacrifice. The monsters were waiting."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "People and beasts attacked them. Griffith was taken away."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot talk about it now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About our friends."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Griffith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what comes next."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Nothing yet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have to correct what I told you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How many people did you lose?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Dead?.. All of them?.. Who attacked them?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I saw the ceremony. People were given to monsters. Griffith stood at its center."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wait... Griffith? Are you saying he knew what they would do to them? Knew beforehand?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know what was in his mind. I saw what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I try to picture him there, beside all that... and I cannot. He knew their names. Every one. They followed him through more than I could count."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then tell me what you saw. No more. I do not want guesses, even if they might be easier to live with."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need time. I hear you. What I remember of him does not fit your words yet. That is not your fault."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not believe me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you like to be alone?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for telling me. I do not know what else to say."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am not saying you are lying. I am trying to understand how the person I knew, or thought I knew, could do that. It is not the same thing."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For a little while. We will talk again. I will not hide from it forever."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I keep remembering his words, trying to understand when we stopped being people to him and became steps. A price. I have no answer."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you want to find him?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want to hear him answer. Ask him to his face: why? What I would do after hearing it... I do not know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Today I can finish the work I started. My hands at least know what to do. Tomorrow I will try to understand the rest. One day at a time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then he might still be alive?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know what became of him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Looking for him now would be pointless."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not ask any more."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then I cannot count him among the lost yet. Not until I know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now, perhaps. But if you find a trace, I want to know. Straight away."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Enough for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me as soon as you learn something. I need to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Which part was a lie?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The attackers. And Griffith being taken. He took part in what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You saw me asking about him. Hoping to find him. Clinging to that hope. And you left me with that story?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I chose what you should know. I was wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I could not say it. You should not have had to live with a lie."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would it have been easier if you kept believing?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You could have said you could not talk yet. I would have waited. Now tell me. All of it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell him everything I witnessed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You could have asked for time. I would have given it. Tell me now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need to decide what to do with the truth myself. Do not choose what is easier for me again. You have no right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you trust me again?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not straight away. But you came back and told me yourself. That counts for something. We will see what you do next."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I will not force the words out of you. Just do not tell me everything is all right if it is not."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can talk now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still not ready."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then let us do something else for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot give an honest count. No one called the roll afterwards. They are people to me, not a tally."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you saw. I was not there; I will not pretend to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "They offered me strength. I refused and left as a human."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know how to put that right. But I can listen. You do not have to explain everything today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Judeau."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He noticed when someone was struggling, and helped without making them feel foolish. You could ask him things you were ashamed not to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I found his remains."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what happened to him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show the object found beside him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you found. No comforting inventions. I want to remember the truth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted you to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know if it really belonged to him. Thank you for bringing it to show me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you like to keep it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I just wanted you to see it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. If you are ready to part with it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Give him the keepsake."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will keep it for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Pippin."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He said little. I would still be explaining what needed moving or holding, then see he had already done it. I felt less afraid beside him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I kept thinking he might have escaped. I was so used to him bearing more than anyone else. It seemed nothing could break him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Corkus."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not always easy to get along with. One bitter remark could ruin a day. Then he would say something so absurd you could not stay angry."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I never expected to miss his grumbling. Now I try to remember his voice and cannot get it quite right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He had plans for life after the marches. He spoke of them so often I knew them by heart. Listening, I could believe we would live like people one day."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He spoke of the future as if it were already within reach. It is hard to accept it stayed only a conversation by a campfire."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Whom did you want to talk about?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you. I will keep it safe."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Go ahead. Just mind the cloth with the parts on it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you ever get frightened?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you could choose what to work on?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does it bother you that others are stronger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good talking with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course. Especially when there is nothing left to check or tighten, my hands have no work, and my head keeps imagining the worst."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you do then?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It does not always show."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I try not to be entirely alone with it. We do not even have to talk. Sometimes someone sitting nearby is enough."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I work with my hands. From outside, being busy may look like being calm. They are not always the same."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would still make things. Things that make living easier, not only surviving."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Weapons help people survive too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A mounting you can work with after an injury. A cart you do not have to drag out of every rut. Even a lock that does not jam in the cold."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. That is why I make them. Sometimes I want to make something for after the battle, too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sometimes. Especially when someone is trapped and I cannot move what fell on them. You stand there, hands shaking, unable to help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How do you deal with it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I learn what I can. Try to find a way to help before things become that bad, while there is still time to prevent it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. I have decided. We can talk about work, but not traveling together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where are you going? And what do you expect of me if I agree?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We would help each other. I do not want to go alone."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I could use your knowledge. The choice is yours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know yet. Let us talk later."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You will do as I say. I do not need an assistant who argues."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come with me, or you will regret it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your friends were weak. Be useful to me and perhaps you will outlive them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About your decision."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can shoot, watch the equipment, help on the road. But if we are walking toward pointless death, I will say so."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will listen."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We can argue. We will decide together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I said you will obey."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am glad you say that. But I do not want to come only to mend equipment while you decide everything else. My word has to mean something."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am asking you to be a companion."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I understand. Think about it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I feed you for your help. You will obey."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then tell me where you want to go first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First, supplies and a safe road."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "To the lair we know. We will scout the approaches first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before setting out, let us discuss what is happening to me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we set out, tell me what is happening to you. I need to know what to expect beside you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I will come. Let me gather my things and tell Godot; I do not want him wondering where I went."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will tell you about the change."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I changed my mind. We will stay for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Better to agree now than sort it out on the road when it is too late to turn back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will be ready soon. I will not keep you long."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us discuss equipment and travel arrangements."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then you need someone else. I will not go with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You can order work from me. You cannot buy me. That ends the talk about traveling together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. After those words, I am not going anywhere with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not speak of them that way. Do not imagine I would walk beside someone who can say that."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I was wrong to speak to you that way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you at least finish my order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for saying so. But I have not changed my decision."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How are you holding up?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you think of our road?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About our equipment."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I just wanted to know how you are."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am hurt. Let us find somewhere quiet and look at the wounds before going farther."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am holding up. When we can, I want to check the crossbow without rushing. On the road I keep worrying about something I missed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would like to know where we are going. If it is just looking for supplies, say so. That is worthwhile too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Supplies first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have a lead to a lair."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we get closer, let us look for a way to retreat if things go wrong. I am happier seeing a way back before I need it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ah... I see. Not always well, honestly. Thank you for asking. Not everyone notices the difference."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Want to talk?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We could just sit a while."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Something ordinary first, though, not the hardest things at once."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Were you going to tell me what is happening to you? Or was I meant to guess?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you know about this change."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I accepted the power."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I did not know how to start."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is none of your business."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know what I will become."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not need to understand. Just obey."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then tell me what you were promised. And what you understand yourself, beyond somebody else's words."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I accepted strength. I will not treat people as possessions."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still need help with my hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Start with what you know for certain. We can work through the rest as we go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When we walk side by side, it concerns me too. I need to know what to expect, so I can survive beside you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You can keep your own counsel. But before I travel with you, I need to know what to expect."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then do not hide changes from me. Tell me before it is too late. I cannot promise to stop it, but I want to understand you while I still can."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We can keep talking. My choice about the road is still mine."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us discuss the road as companions."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. That was not our agreement when I chose to come with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Can you still hold a tool comfortably with that hand?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does that plate get in the way when you bend? You seem to move differently."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will walk behind you in narrow passages. I do not want to get in the way if you have to turn or spread those wings."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have you noticed my hands?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The shell has changed how I move."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The wings make things cramped."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I will be here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Until next time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good luck. Bring them and we will carry on."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Thank you for staying with me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "So was I. We can talk without something being broken first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "So was I. Visit without broken equipment sometimes. Give me a rest from other people's repairs."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Enough for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have not introduced ourselves yet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert, by the way. And your name?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Introduce yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good to meet you. Mind the parts on the cloth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still busy with your crossbow?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You would not believe how much time one lousy part the size of a fingernail can eat."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Take up a sword. Fewer parts: iron and an edge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can barely lift your sword off the table. I will keep my little parts. Safer that way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I hear you. What I remember of him does not fit your words yet. I need time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could I assemble the mechanism myself?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When we can, I want to check the crossbow without rushing. On the road I keep worrying about something I missed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why did you take me in?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I think so. First a mounting that holds without pressing on the wound. Then the mechanical hand and the small barrel inside."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I understand what you mean."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will remember that."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We will follow the lead we know and scout the approaches first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We will look around before going farther."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About trusting me after my lie."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My hand has grown back. What about my order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You no longer need a replacement hand. I still have the materials you brought; you can take them back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You no longer need a replacement hand. Let us close that order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Close the order and collect any materials delivered."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember the lie. But I have had time to listen to you since then. We can talk about the road again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "After what came out, I need time. I can work beside you at the forge. Trusting you with my life on the road is another matter."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us talk honestly about what I saw and what I mean to do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About traveling together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not try to mend this with another fine promise. Keep speaking honestly until I can see it is a habit."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for sitting down and telling me plainly. I cannot forget everything at once. Let us leave it there for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know you well enough to leave everything and go with you. Come back and talk; we will see how things go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How can I rebuild your trust?"
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your flesh grows thick and heavy. Gain +3 strength and 3 points of natural protection. You remain slower, and gas can still hurt you. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The thickened body cannot fit ordinary rigid torso and leg armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your heavy, pliant body grants +3 strength and 3 points of natural protection. Your slower movement remains. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. It does not heal wounds.\n\nClothing: The swollen torso and arms cannot fit ordinary rigid armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent pliant body grants +1 strength and 2 points of natural protection, with another -5 speed. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The thickened torso cannot fit ordinary rigid armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Dark wings lighten your movements. Gain +2 strength, +1 dexterity, +10 speed and 2 points of natural protection; falling damage is halved. The wings do not allow sustained flight. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The wings need an open back; ordinary torso clothing gets in their way."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent fiery carapace grants +3 strength, 6 points of natural protection, -15 speed and 50% less heat damage. Hunger and slow recovery remain. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. It does not heal wounds or make fire harmless.\n\nClothing: The carapace cannot fit beneath ordinary rigid torso or limb armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent carapace grants +1 strength, 3 points of natural protection and 25% less heat damage, with another -8 speed. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The carapace cannot fit beneath ordinary rigid torso or arm armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanently grown insectlike wings grant +2 dexterity, +15 speed and half falling damage. Wings permit gliding with a light load and usable arms, not free ascent into the sky. Torso encumbrance above 20 prevents your wing abilities. Your fragile flesh remains. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The wings need an open back; ordinary torso clothing gets in their way."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent insectlike body grants +1 dexterity and +8 speed. Its fragility and difficulties with speech and crafting remain. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The insectlike head and hands do not fit ordinary rigid helmets, masks or gloves."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanently altered flesh grants +4 strength, +1 dexterity, +15% melee damage and 4 points of natural protection. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. Its growth does not heal wounds.\n\nClothing: Rigid sleeves and gauntlets cannot follow the reshaped flesh."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your outline becomes difficult to follow. Gain +2 dexterity and reduce your visibility range by 3 tiles. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: Ordinary rigid helmets and masks do not fit the altered head."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "A fragile, elongated shape sharpens perception of distance. Gain +2 dexterity, +1 dodge and 1 point of natural protection. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: Elongated fingers do not fit ordinary rigid gloves."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your beastlike body grants +3 strength, +15% melee damage and -2 dexterity. Your stamina still recovers slowly. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. It does not heal wounds.\n\nClothing: The changed hands and feet cannot fit ordinary rigid gloves and footwear."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent beastlike body grants +2 strength and -2 dexterity. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The changed hands cannot fit ordinary rigid gloves."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Bone presses through the scar. Tendons tighten, fingers uncurl: your left hand has grown back."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "A mechanical cannon attached to the left forearm. Deploy it to wield and reload its single chamber, then retract it to use another weapon. It burns powder charges instead of bionic power."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your hand has grown back. Speak with Rickert at the forge to settle the unnecessary prosthesis order and collect any materials already delivered."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your hand has grown back. You no longer need a replacement."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You are on your feet, swordsman. After that night, that is no small thing."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You can stand again. Then the time I won for you that night was not wasted."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Was there something else you wanted to ask?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I will hear your questions."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Was it you who carried me out?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I want to understand what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Tell me about the Brand and those who come at night."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will you help me?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Where should I look for this evil now?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found something among the remains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "It is time for me to go."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "That is enough for now. I will speak to you again."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found an opening and carried you through before it closed. But carrying a body out of a place of sacrifice does not free it from the sacrifice itself."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Yes. You were among those who were not meant to leave that ceremony alive. I carried you out. The people where you woke did the rest."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I carried you somewhere I could leave you safely. We did not reach the woodland forge."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Because of this mark?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Griffith. What became of him?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What happened to me?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Who are these people?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What do I need to know first?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Was saving your life not help enough?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot and Rickert. You have already spoken with both of them. They sheltered you when I brought you here."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You know Godot. The young craftsman at his forge is Rickert; you have yet to meet him yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot is a smith. Rickert works beside him on crossbows and mechanisms. You will have to meet them for yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You saw the boundary where greatness is bought with other lives. Those who rose above the crowd accepted that harvest. Those feasting beneath the throne merely did what they had been permitted."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Were those creatures once human?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "And those who stood above them?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why is this happening among our cities?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can things be put back as they were?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What became of Griffith?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can the one who presided over this do it again?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Many were. They rejected their nature when an earthly existence was no longer enough. Their old failings and desires remained. Sometimes those human habits make the monsters recognizable. And vulnerable."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can they be destroyed?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Their altered flesh can be destroyed. Do not mistake their bodies for true immortality. Nor should you look for human mercy where the abyss rules."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "How do I fight them with ordinary weapons?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Wait before you step forward. Study how the enemy moves, what it protects and when it must pause for breath. Know where you will retreat. Blind fury is no substitute for a way back."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The God Hand. Do not confuse them with the servants admitted to the feast. Killing an ordinary apostle does not bring their overthrow a step closer."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then resistance is pointless?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I defeated his reflection. How could he be there again?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "If I thought your struggle useless, I would not have carried you out of that hell."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "This land had already been wounded by its own end of the world. Another darkness seeps through the open wounds. The boundary has thinned, making your home accessible to hungrier predators."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The past cannot be restored, even if every passage is sealed. But you can keep the next traveler from meeting the same fate."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "He took the throne offered to him. Your memories of the man cannot explain the abyss into which he was reborn."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I do not care what he became. I will reach his throat."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then first learn to live until the next dawn. Otherwise your oath of vengeance will be no more than the last words of a man dying in the night."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Do not expect what you witnessed to be the last expression of that will. Your concern now is to endure the threat already following you."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You dispersed a reflection. It could take his shape and carry some of his power, but it was not the being you seek."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then that fight meant nothing?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "How can I distinguish a reflection from the original?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will there be more reflections?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The shape that stood before you will threaten no one else. That matters. But do not credit your victory with something it did not accomplish."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "A face is not enough. Consider where it came from, what holds it here and what it leaves behind. A vanished shadow is not proof of an original death."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "While the boundaries between worlds remain broken, I would not call that encounter the last."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The Brand remains a mark of sacrifice. Beings beyond the boundary can discern it where a human eye sees nothing. Night makes their journey to you easier."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Does it warn me of danger?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will they come every night?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What should I do before dark?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "How can I protect my refuge?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will closing a breach remove the Brand?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Pain and blood may come before a creature appears, especially a powerful one. Heed that warning, but do not expect it to name your enemy or show a safe road. The Brand is no friend to you. It simply is."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Not every night is the same. Sometimes you will hear only footsteps beyond a wall. Sometimes you will have to abandon your shelter and run. Silence does not mean they have forgotten you."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Find a place you can leave. Do not corner yourself for the imagined safety of walls. Prepare light, dressings and weapons. Keep what you need close: there will be no time to pack when you must flee."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will a locked door help?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will they disappear in the morning?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Against some of them, yes. But an ordinary wall cannot keep out everything that comes from the darkness. Some creatures need no door."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Dawn may end the pursuit itself. It does not promise to destroy those that already reached you. Look at what remains outside before opening the door."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "There are signs that hinder their approach. I will leave you the instructions. But a sign cannot replace shelter: choose somewhere you can defend and leave."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You have already begun preparing. Wise. But do not mistake that sign for a fortress wall. It will not destroy a creature already beside you; it hinders the way here."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then I can sleep peacefully?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Tell me how to arrange it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "More peacefully. Not carelessly. Even a protected place must have an exit. Never make the sign your last hope."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Arrange eight stones and four bones into a sign on clear ground. Keep it close to your sleeping place. Its protection stays on the same level; it will not drive away creatures already here."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "No. You will close one road into this world, and that matters to those who live nearby. The mark on your body belongs to another bond. Closing a breach does not break it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The trail leads to the forest hollow. The direction is already in your records. Prepare before following it; I will not choose your next step for you."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Victory left you more than a dead enemy. Examine what remains in its lair. You may find why it came to these lands."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You have found the trail of a passage. Now deal with the wound itself. A fallen keeper does not always mean the road behind it has closed."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The roads you learned are already marked. Follow an unfinished trail when you are ready. You need not take on every enemy at once."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You have exhausted the trails you had. Revisit the evidence and speak with those you trust. The next road remains to be discovered; I will not point you toward something I do not know."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "First let your wounds close. Speak with the craftsmen, gather what you need and prepare for night. The road will not disappear while you learn to walk it without falling at the first step."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found judeau's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about judeau."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Judeau saw other people even when everything around him was turning them into prey."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found pippin's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about pippin."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Sometimes a man knows he cannot hold the enemy. Still he stands between it and those who can escape."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found corkus's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about corkus."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "A victim has a life that cannot fit inside the word victim. Desires, failings, arguments. Do not give the monsters that part of him as well."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found gaston's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Such hopes are easily lost behind banners and the names of commanders. To him that future mattered no less than another man's dream of a kingdom."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Tell me what you found."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "It was not enough."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Not enough to stop all that happened. But you do not know how much time his act gave someone else."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I want him remembered."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then preserve more than how he died. Preserve who he was."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You call that victory?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I call it an act that cannot be measured only by who remained standing."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I should have been beside him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You may carry that thought all your life. It cannot put you beside him that night. Decide whom you will stand beside now."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "We often disagreed."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Grief does not require that you agreed on everything in life."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "He was no hero."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "They did not need to become heroes to deserve their lives."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "That makes it harder."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Yes. You see not only a death but everything that can never follow it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What should I do with the keepsake?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Keep it, give it to someone who knew him, or leave it in a worthy place. Memory does not demand you always carry its weight."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "One who has long walked against them."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "That is no name."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why did you save me?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why did you not save the others?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Were you once human too?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can fate be changed?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why will you not stay?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "No. But for now it tells you more than a name."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I had the chance to intervene. I took it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "And you want nothing in return?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I did not carry you out of one bargain to immediately bind you to another."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Because I could not."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "But you knew what was happening."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I cannot accept that."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Knowing of a disaster and having the power to stop it are not the same."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I am not asking you to accept it. But do not base your next step on the belief that someone could have fixed everything with a single blow."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Enough humanity remains in me to remember what I fight against."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "And the rest?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Not every story needs to be told at another man's threshold."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You are alive and asking that question. Begin there."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then everything depends on my choice?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "No. But your choice still belongs to you. Do not give it away merely because you cannot rule everything else."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I have my own road. Our enemies will not wait for you to recover."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will we meet again?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Perhaps. But do not build your life around waiting for me."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Have you finished?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then know this: I will continue my journey. If you still have questions, ask them now. Do not expect me to return to this threshold."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Wait. I have more questions."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Remind me of the essentials."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I understand. Farewell."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Prepare for night. Ask the craftsmen for what you lack. Then follow a trail you know. Do not try to settle your whole war in a single battle."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Recover before another fight. Prepare what you need, and follow a trail you already know."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Farewell."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then preserve the life with which you intend to continue."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Live on. What kind of life it will be is yours to decide."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Watch the rider leave."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Words recorded after speaking with the Skull Knight."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Close the record."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What else did you want to ask?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The Knight carried me out of the sacrifice. Escape did not undo its consequences."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot works on blades; Rickert works on crossbows and mechanisms. A road marker is not a personal acquaintance."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "A bone and stone sign hinders the Brand's night summons nearby. It does not remove creatures already here and does not replace shelter."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Recover before a fight. Directions are kept as ordinary missions and map markers; the road journal is only a reference."
msgstr ""

#. Direct mission routes 2026-10-22
msgid "The wound cools and its heartbeat stops. This place is quieter. The defenders' surviving marks reveal three trails: the Count's residence, the Black Dogs' camp and a misty valley."
msgstr ""

#. Direct mission routes 2026-10-22
msgid "Notes about known places, the smiths' work and what you have learned. It is a reference: your missions and map markers remain if this book is lost."
msgstr ""

#. Direct mission routes 2026-10-22
msgid "A new objective is marked on your map."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot works on blades; Rickert works on crossbows and mechanisms at the woodland forge."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Recover before a fight. Prepare for night, then follow a trail you know. Do not take on every enemy at once."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I wanted to ask about someone else who died."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Read the entries"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "I lost my road notes. Could I have a new notebook?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Find the predator in the marked hollow. Inspect the approaches and the ruined stopping place, prepare a way back, then defeat the creature. After the fight, examine the traces and belongings left in its lair."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Defeat the keeper at the marked breach, then examine the wound at its center. Closing the passage will not destroy creatures which have already crossed. Study the surviving marks for further trails."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "The Count's residence"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Explore the marked residence and the rooms below its execution hall. The trail leads to the Count and a passage held open beneath his house. Deal with the keeper, examine the wound and recover what remains after it is sealed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "The Black Dogs' camp"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Follow the trail to the Black Dogs' camp. Inspect its stores, prisoners' traces and paths of retreat. Wyald holds this place; after confronting him, find the wound linked to the camp and examine what remains when it closes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Follow the marked trail into the valley. The evidence names Rosine. Study the flowers, cocoons and paths before confronting her. Examine the wound linked to this place and recover the surviving relic after it closes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Grunbeld's stronghold"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "The surviving trail leads to the stronghold. Explore the fortifications and the passage linked to this place. Grunbeld's fate depends on the earlier encounter; examine the evidence you find here, close the wound and recover what remains."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Bring Godot 8 lumps of high steel, 600 charcoal and 4 leather patches. After delivery, allow two days for forging and tempering."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Return to Godot two days after the last delivery and collect your finished blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Return to Godot twelve hours after delivering the materials and collect the battle sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Traces in the empty lair"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "The predator is dead. Examine the traces in its lair: the ash and abandoned belongings may preserve a trail to the place it came from. If you recovered the burned scrap, you can study it as well."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "The surviving trail leads to the stronghold. Explore the fortifications and the passage linked to this place. Examine the traces Grunbeld left here, close the wound and recover what remains."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Where can I find that forge?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot looks at your blade, then raises his eyes. \"Guts. Thought I would recognize you by that iron when I could no longer make out your face. What is it? Straighten your sword again?\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&The smith turns the billet in his tongs. Only after a few hammer blows does he notice you. \"Close the door. And step away from that bucket.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot taps the anvil without turning. \"Another soldier full of stories. A sword is a tool. It must be balanced and quick. Too heavy, and you will die winding up for the first swing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot turns the sword, checks the grip and draws a thumb across the edge. \"Someone took pains with this. Still a long way from a fine blade, but better than nothing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot checks the grip and the edge. \"What matters is how it behaves in the hand. You worked at it, I can see. A long way from a fine blade, but better than nothing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot clears a space beside the enormous black blade. \"Finished. Come around and help me shift it. A blade for things a man was never meant to fight. Your Dragonslayer.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot lifts the white-hot billet from the forge. Light crosses his worn face. The hammer falls; sparks scatter across the dark earthen floor. \"What do you see before you?\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot returns to the iron. He does not resume the conversation."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "&Godot turns back to the anvil. \"Enough talk. The iron is cooling.\""
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "An enormous beastlike figure. Its presence feels solid, but the edges of its body keep fading in and out."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "The %s loses its outline and dissolves."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "A motionless winged image. Its face is clearer than the rest of its body."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "An inhuman figure that seems to bend straight lines around it."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "A heavy figure with human features. Its edges tremble like an image in muddy water."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "A beastlike figure with a broad grin. Its outline lags behind its sudden movements."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "A winged silhouette hovers above the ground. The space behind it shows through the thin edges of its wings."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "An image enclosed in a heavy carapace. Heat glimmers in its cracks without casting the light it should."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "An image of living flesh held in an alien space. Its movements are too smooth for its blurred outline."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "A small floating figure. Look away, and it becomes hard to remember exactly where it was."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "A squat image amid a cloudy suspension. Its contours slowly emerge, then dissolve again."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "About the strange stone and the changes."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "You are looking at me strangely. Is something wrong?"
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "Before you hand me the armor..."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "I came to collect the finished blade."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "I found belongings among the dead."
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "How do I live with this change?"
msgstr ""

#. Named apostles 2026-10-23
msgid "Did you want to ask something before we set out?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "the Count's prisoner"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I just want to get out of here alive."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The master and his followers leave you and your companions alone while the pact holds. An attack from your side will break it. This truce gives you no command over demons."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Threadbreaker"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You survived an impossible battle and kept your humanity. Strength +8, dexterity, intelligence and perception +4, speed +25; maximum health and stamina increased by half. This mark of victory will stay with you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Truce: the Count"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "An active pact protects this companion. Their body remains unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Truce: Wyald"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Truce: Rosine"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Truce: Grunbeld"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Service to the Count"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I need two pieces of leather for the household stores. Bring them here. Then you will be able to call on the tendril's strength again."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Spoils for the Black Dogs"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Bring twelve pieces of scrap metal to equip the Dogs. Let's see if you can bring back spoils instead of just running your mouth. With my help, you can charge ahead and sweep aside anyone nearby."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Supplies for the Nest"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Bring four pieces of meat for the nest. Then I'll help you move more lightly, slipping away from others' blows for a little while."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld's Commission"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Deliver four lumps of steel. They are needed to repair armor. In return, I will help you harden your shell for a short time; moving under blows will become harder."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Collect the Repaired Blade"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You left your blade with Godo. Return to the forest forge two hours after handing it over and ask for your weapon back. The materials have already been supplied."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Materials for Crossbow Bolts"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "To make ten crossbow bolts, Rickert needs 1 lump of steel, 1 stick, 20 units of thread, 10 feathers and 50 units of charcoal. Give the full set to Rickert himself at the forest forge. The work will take half an hour after delivery."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Collect Rickert's Bolts"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert has the materials for ten bolts. Return to him at the forest forge half an hour after delivery and collect the finished work."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "locked iron grille"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A heavy wrought-iron grille. A lock holds it in the stone doorway."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You finish sawing through the iron bars."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "open iron grille"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The iron grille has been pushed aside. The doorway is clear."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "iron grille"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A heavy iron grille blocks the doorway. Its lock is unfastened."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A scar where the passage closed. Living tissue trembles beneath your feet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Examine the relic"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A plain iron key. It locked the west-wing cell and the service passage between the records office and the execution hall."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora's paper charm. The scent of dried herbs still lingers in its fibers."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Examine the charm"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A notebook of travel notes. It holds known places, the names of people you have met and information worth keeping. Your quests and map markers stay with you even if the book is lost."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You've come back. How was the road?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wounded: \"Sit down before you start telling me. You're favoring a wound; I can see it in the way you move.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No significant change: \"Your place by the hearth is free.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "First return with the Brand: \"Something terrible has happened to you since we last met. Tell me when you're ready, and not before.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Received her armor: \"How are you managing with the armor? It isn't easy on you, I know.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Come in. You can leave the mud and your road-weary worries at the door. Though the latter are usually harder to shed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My name is Guts. I was told you could help."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I didn't expect to find a home here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I was told a witch named Flora lives here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I wanted to talk."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And I don't expect every traveler to appear on this path. My name is Flora. Are you lost, or looking for someone?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I was looking for shelter."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I saw the tree and decided to come closer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I need help."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you live here alone?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then rest first. Questions come more easily when you stop listening for every rustle behind you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It draws the attention of those who look around them, rather than only at their own feet. I hope the road here treated you kindly."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me what kind. I can't promise to solve everything in the world, but I can listen."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "This house is rarely entirely alone. But right now you're speaking to its mistress."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm Flora. Sit down, Guts. You're holding yourself as though you expect a blow even here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Habit."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A useful one on the road. You can let it rest for a little while here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then you've come to the right place. Who showed you the way?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I found a note with your name in it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Someone told me about you on the road."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Show me, if you wish. Sometimes another person's words travel a long way before bringing someone to my door."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then we'll see how kindly those rumors have treated us both."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Don't linger. The path is still holding."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There is a presence bound to you that I did not expect. More than the trace of someone else's touch. Did you accept the power you were offered?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You needn't bring a misfortune to my door. Sometimes simple curiosity is enough."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What did you want to talk about?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can you sense what happened to me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I did it to survive."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That's my business."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to ask about the Brand."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What are these creatures from another world?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Let's talk about the armor."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me about this house and the tree."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I learned of a danger..."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "May I ask about you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Something strange has happened to me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've finished preparing. Let's continue."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Which way should I go?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll stay and fight."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can I save anything?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Thank you for answering honestly. Then we'll have to talk about what is changing now, both for you and for the help I am willing to offer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't know everything you have been through. But it is you who must face the consequences. It isn't for me to judge whether the price justifies what was done."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your choice. But I am responsible for the help I give here, and I must decide what I am willing to offer and what I am not."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What troubles you about the Brand?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That mark binds you to what happened during the sacrifice. It remains visible to beings an ordinary person might not even notice."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is that how they find me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can you remove it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why does it hurt more around some creatures?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why is it quieter here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I already have a protective sign."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Did closing the breach change nothing? The Brand is still there."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes. Especially when night makes the boundary between your world and their presence less distinct."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. I can help you protect yourself and better understand what is happening. But promising to remove the Brand would be cruel of me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Does that mean it's forever?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can you at least ease the pain?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know no way to free you from it. That is the limit of my knowledge, not a reason to stop caring for your life."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Sometimes the danger causing it can be reduced. But don't silence every warning merely because it hurts. Pain is sometimes the only warning that reaches you in time."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Their presence varies. Some barely touch our world. Others bring such power that your body senses it before you can see its source."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So the pain tells me how strong an enemy is?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It tells you to be more careful. But pain is a poor measuring instrument. Don't test its limits with your life."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The tree and the wards around the house make it harder for many beings to approach. I have tended this place for a long time; decades, to be quite honest."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Am I safe here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "How can I prepare protection somewhere else?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You can rest here. But I wouldn't call any house beyond the reach of every power. That would be presumptuous of me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A sign of stone and bone hinders the beings the Brand calls. Keep it near your resting place. It won't drive away those already here, or replace a way out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then you have done something important: prepared a place to return to."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is that enough?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The sign is no substitute for walls, vigilance or a way out, especially once a creature is already close. Protection serves those who understand its limits better than those who rely on it blindly."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It did change something. You denied those creatures one way in. The people nearby may never know why things grew quieter, but that doesn't make your work futile."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And for me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "For you, the Brand remains. A closed wound in the world and the mark on your body are different things. One does not undo the other."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Human senses show only a part of what exists. There are beings and powers for which our familiar walls, distances and even shapes don't mean quite what they mean to us."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Another world hidden inside ours?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are all its inhabitants dangerous?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why is everything mixing together now?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can all the rifts be closed?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That is one way to begin imagining it. Just don't think of it as a neighboring room always reached through the same door."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. But unfamiliar kindness and unfamiliar danger can look equally puzzling at first. That is why curiosity should walk beside caution, not ahead of it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The world you lived in has already suffered a catastrophe. Now we are seeing something else penetrate its damaged boundaries. I have studied this for a long time, but I still cannot explain every case."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So you don't know what comes next either?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't. Knowledge begins with a willingness to admit where understanding ends, rather than with a confident voice."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It would take an immense effort. Find them, understand what keeps each open, reach those hidden from sight. No one should mistake that task for a short journey. It could take a lifetime, and even that might not be enough."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Where should I begin, then?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "With the place you already know about. Help where you can truly act, instead of only imagining the weight of all that lies ahead. Thinking about that weight alone won't lighten the world's burden."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you want to discuss: what it does, its consequences, or how to manage it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Armor that lets its wearer keep fighting when their own body is already demanding that they stop."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "How does it work?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "At what price?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why do you keep it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will you let me take it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I already have the armor."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I lost the pieces you gave me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will you help me complete the set?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "May I have the armor?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Pain and fear keep us from making certain movements. The body has those safeguards for a reason. The armor helps you cross those limits. But an injury doesn't vanish because you can no longer feel it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Does it heal wounds?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Don't mistake being able to move for being healed. After the battle, the body must still endure what happened to it. A delay is no reprieve."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "At first the price may seem small: fatigue, pain that you will feel later, once it is over. The greater danger is growing used to treating any injury as acceptable while an enemy remains. That habit is more dangerous than the pain itself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Sometimes stopping isn't an option."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What if I use it only as a last resort?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I stop telling friends from enemies?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know. That is why I want you to distinguish necessity from merely wanting to continue. They are not the same, though the heat of battle blurs the difference."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then decide what counts as a last resort beforehand. In the fight itself, that definition has a way of quietly changing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rage narrows the world. Anything that keeps it from its goal begins to look like an obstacle, friend or otherwise. Don't wait for that to happen before thinking of those who will fight beside you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will help me hold on?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Remember why you come back from a battle. Listen to those you trust. And notice the moment when you no longer want to stop, though the reason for fighting is long gone."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Because there are dangers ordinary means may not be enough to face. Hiding a dangerous thing and calling the matter settled is not enough. You must understand who might truly need it, and why."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I will, if you understand what you're asking. I don't demand a promise that you will never make a mistake. But I want to hear why you need that strength."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "To endure what ordinary armor can't."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "To protect those who are still alive."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "To reach the one who did all this."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I haven't decided yet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll go on without the armor."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then remember: standing your ground and coming back are not always the same. Care about the second as much as the first."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Hold on to those words. Especially on the day your enemy seems more important than those you're protecting."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I hear your resolve. But I won't call revenge a protection from the armor's price. Those are different things, however much you wish to make them one."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then take your time. You can stay here and think for as long as you need."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Now let's talk about something else. Where you will go next, with armor or without it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "All right. I will help you with the armor. Don't leave before you're sure you know how to handle it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm ready to accept it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "One more question first."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll return to this later."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You brought a piece of the armor. Let me see what's missing.\n\nI can help with what you still lack. And we'll discuss the whole suit before you decide to rely on it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm ready to accept the missing pieces."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You already have the armor. I won't pretend I can undo everything that has happened. But please don't treat two dangerous powers as cures for each other. Together, they may cost you far more than either alone."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You already have the armor. But obtaining it doesn't mean you have learned to stand against it. If you wish, we can discuss what it will demand in return."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What should I watch for in myself?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What should I do after a hard battle?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've already used it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Don't mistake being able to move for being healed. After the battle, the body must still endure what happened to it. A delay is no reprieve.\n\nAt first the price may seem small: fatigue, pain that you will feel later, once it is over. The greater danger is growing used to treating any injury as acceptable while an enemy remains. That habit is more dangerous than the pain itself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then tell me: was it harder to start fighting, or to stop?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "To stop."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I stayed in control."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't want to talk about it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It is good that you noticed. Don't dismiss that feeling once the wounds heal. It will return, and next time it may be stronger."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "May it stay that way. Just don't treat one successful battle as a promise for every one that follows."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You needn't tell me. But answer it for yourself. Sooner or later, you must."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've already given you what I could. I don't have another set like it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I will not give you the armor. You have already allowed another power to change your body. I won't add another will's hold over it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you think I'm a monster?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "But I can still protect people."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then there's nothing for me here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I am speaking of what I do not wish to aid, not of who you are. You came here in peace, and I am still talking to you. That already means something."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You can. And I hope you will. That doesn't oblige me to give you every dangerous thing in my house."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You can rest here, ask questions and decide where to go. My door was not opened only for the sake of the armor, and it remains open to you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Refusal does not always leave a person unhurt. But a wound inflicted on you doesn't mean you agreed to it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can you put this right?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I can listen and help you understand what has changed. I won't promise a healing I do not know. That would be a lie."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me what help you need."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you have anything that might help against apostles?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "May I take supplies for the road?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "About the prepared supplies."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There are bundles prepared for you in the kitchen, workshop and south gallery. Take them if they will help you on the road. Leave the other things where they are."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Thank you. I'll take only what you've set aside."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You may take the bundles I prepared. No new supplies will appear in their place, so use them carefully."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Because this place became possible beside it. I built the house trying not to quarrel with the roots. Some parts worked better than others; some had to be rebuilt. The tree is more headstrong than any customer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Does it protect you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is it an ordinary tree?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Everything here looks too ordinary."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why do you need so many books?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Have you lived here long?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It helps protect this place. And I care for it. I like to think being neighbors should mean giving as well as taking."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It lives within more connections at once than the trees you are used to seeing by the road. Its roots touch more than earth."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can you talk to it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You can start by sitting quietly beside it. Not every conversation needs human words."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Were you expecting more skulls and bubbling cauldrons?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Probably."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It's just that everything is different outside."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I like it here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm afraid I must disappoint you. My cauldron is more often needed for supper than for anything sinister."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That makes it all the more important to find a cup, a dry towel and a place by the fire here. That difference offers a kind of protection too."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then the house is doing its job."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So I mistake my own memory for something infallible a little less often. And because some people leave only books behind them. Nothing else remains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Long enough to stop noticing some of the creaking floorboards. Guests remind me of them better than any clock."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're avoiding the question."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A little. An old person's habit, when she sometimes wants to talk about something other than her age."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Ask."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Aren't you afraid of me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why do you help strangers?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you know the Skull Knight?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't have time to sit by the hearth."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't understand why this is happening to me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If I leave, can I come back?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The power beside you is dangerous. I can feel it; there's no need to pretend.\n\nBut it isn't the only thing I look at. I watch how you use it.\n\nDon't force me to choose between a guest and this house. I would make that choice quickly, and not in your favor."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Afraid?\n\nYou came into my home. You asked me to listen. For now, that matters more than any fear."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Strangers for now. A stranger today needn't be one tomorrow.\n\nAnd sometimes it's simpler than that. They have nowhere else to go."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I do. For a long time now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can he be trusted?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Does he always talk like that?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Who was he?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He doesn't tell everything. Ever. Even if you ask three times.\n\nBut if he pulled you out, don't belittle that just because answers didn't come with it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I suppose he has little choice. Habit is a tenacious thing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That is his story, not mine. One day he'll decide whom to tell. I won't tell it for him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That is his story, not mine. If you want to know, ask him. I won't tell it for him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Perhaps.\n\nBut you're sitting here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Not for long."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That's usually how it starts."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know no words that would make this fair. Perhaps there are none.\n\nBut here you needn't prove anything. Not that you're coping, nor that you're holding on. You can simply be."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "As long as this house stands and welcomes guests, there will always be a place for you here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me. Not what it looks like; any fool can see that. What happens around it. Who runs, who stays, what the land does in that place.\n\nWhen you go there again, look beyond the creature itself. Look at what it has done to its surroundings. Scorched earth, fallen houses, silence without even a crow's call: these say more than any name people gave it out of fear."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me what you know."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know something about the Count."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know something about Wyald."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know something about Rosine."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know something about Grunbeld."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I closed a breach."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I killed its reflection, or whatever it was."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Where should I go next?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Good work. Hard work.\n\nJust don't mistake quiet for emptiness. The breach closed, but what had already come through it stayed. On this side. Somewhere.\n\nSo don't lower your guard too soon."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It hurt you for real, didn't it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What you cut down was a reflection. It can wound you for real. But its death alone tells you nothing about the fate of the original."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have a known road: the forest hollow.\n\nThe question isn't where. It's whether you're ready to go there now, or should first rest and eat."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have a known road: the ashen rift.\n\nThe question isn't where. It's whether you're ready to go there now, or should first rest and eat."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have a known road: the Count's residence.\n\nThe question isn't where. It's whether you're ready to go there now, or should first rest and eat."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have a known road: the Black Dogs' camp.\n\nThe question isn't where. It's whether you're ready to go there now, or should first rest and eat."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have a known road: the misty valley.\n\nThe question isn't where. It's whether you're ready to go there now, or should first rest and eat."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have a known road: Grunbeld's fortress.\n\nThe question isn't where. It's whether you're ready to go there now, or should first rest and eat."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have nothing. Not no roads; no knowledge.\n\nGo and make sense of what you've already found before stumbling farther at random. Going blindly is like diving headfirst into an ice hole. You might surface, or you might not."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They've passed the first boundary. The guardians are holding, for now. Don't spend that time on questions."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Through the garden to the west, or through the south exit. Watch where you can still get through. The fire won't wait."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Hold back the enemies if you can. But don't stay out of pride. Leaving doesn't mean losing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm staying. The house is my concern.\n\nYours, right now, is getting out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There's a manuscript on the library table. If the way is still clear, take it. If not, leave it and run.\n\nDon't go through fire for it. Do you hear me? Don't."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll try."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There's no way through anymore."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then think no more of it. Paper is paper. You are not."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is something wrong with you? You're looking past me, as if you hear someone behind my back. Before we go on, tell me what's happening."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We've already discussed this."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I accepted a foreign power. It's changing me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Everything's fine. What makes you think that?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Not now. I need to leave."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "All right. Back to work, then."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Don't take me for a fool. I don't know what you let into yourself, but I can see you're trying to hide it. I won't give you a new blade. You can ask for your materials back. They're yours."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll tell you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Have you decided what to do with it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Let's talk about it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is something wrong with you? You keep listening for something. Is it because of that place you came back from?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "All right. Tell me if you need help."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Don't. I'd rather you told me plainly than left me wondering how safe it is to stand beside you. We'll still talk about work. But first I want to hear the truth."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're saying it will continue on its own?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is something wrong with you? I sense unease, but I don't wish to decide for you what it means. Is there anything you want to tell me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Everything is fine. Why do you ask?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Very well. What did you want to discuss?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. There is something behind those words that you're hiding. I won't pass you the armor while you follow this path. But my door remains open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Thank you for telling me. The beginning of a change can still be hidden from the eye. From yourself, perhaps not."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What would you like to discuss?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Look at this stone."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I accepted the power. But I hardly look any different."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My body has begun to change."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've learned something else."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I think my body has stopped changing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I consumed the flesh of a fallen apostle."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "About my pact with the one who changed me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I broke the pact."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The one I served is gone."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I refused the gift, but the consequences remain."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My wings are getting in the way."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "About the shell."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My body has grown heavier."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I remember our conversation. What else?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I wanted to survive."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "To become stronger than any enemy."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'd rather not talk about it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then start by not thinking you're invulnerable."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You haven't seen all your enemies yet. But you've already paid with yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then don't. Just don't expect silence to undo anything."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You move differently. Have you worked out what you can do now?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Test it well away from the forge. And find out how to stop first."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I remember. How are you managing now?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then learn to live with it. The changing is over; there's still work to do."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Killing him wasn't enough for you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I needed his strength."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I wanted to become better than him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have it now. Don't you dare blame a dead man later for what you do yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then start with something besides strength."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So this power has a master. Has he told you what he'll want from you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You've stopped serving him. Good. You'll still have to live with what's left of that bargain."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He won't demand anything of you now. What will you do without his voice in your ear?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You refused, so you refused. Don't let them count you among those who agreed just because you suffered for it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I see it. An ugly face on it. What do you want from me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you know what it is?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. I work iron. I don't have to understand every piece of filth someone brings off the road.\n\nAnd get it off the workbench. People work here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. I work iron. I don't have to understand every piece of filth someone brings off the road."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It's hard for me to speak."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I remember. Has anything changed?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes. And I'll tell you if anything becomes dangerous."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I can handle it myself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then tell me if you notice anything dangerous, especially if we're nearby. I don't want to learn about it when it's too late to step away."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I hope so. But if the consequences affect me, I need to know too."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Did that appear since we last met? Does it hurt?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It hurts."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. It just feels unfamiliar."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I can help with an ordinary dressing, if you need one. But I won't pretend I know how to treat the transformation itself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then take it slowly. Even something that doesn't hurt can get in the way of moving."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me what will happen first. And where I should stand to keep clear."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are you sure? It's good that you at least know what to expect from your own body now. I still need a little time."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Did you know what it would do to you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I didn't know everything."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That's what frightens me. You chose without knowing everything, and now we have to find out the consequences."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "...and now you have to find out the consequences."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to be clear about one thing. Will his orders involve me too?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. You make your own decisions."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If you're coming with me, you'll have to obey."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then remember that if he ever demands otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. I never agreed to serve him through you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then let's at least make sure we understand what's changed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He can't order you about anymore. But I can see your body is still the same... I mean, the way it became because of him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Should I speak louder? Or stand where you can see my face?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me exactly what's become harder. I don't want to guess every time you need help."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "At first I thought it was a carving. But those features... Has it always looked like that?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't know what it is either. Better ask someone who understands these things."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We have spoken about this. Is there anything else?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The beginning isn't always visible from outside. Don't mistake this quiet for a chance to undo what you accepted."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Try describing what has changed before calling it an improvement or a loss. What do you feel? What has become harder?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A new ability can easily become your first answer to every difficulty. Try to keep your other answers too."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are you suggesting I shouldn't use the power?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I am suggesting you notice when you stop choosing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The change has settled into a stable form. Now you must learn it in daily life: in fatigue, hunger, work, and alongside other people."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You brought what remained of a defeated being into your own body. Defeating it does not make that acceptance safe."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You accepted more than a bodily change. You took on an obligation to the one who gave it. What exactly did you promise?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The support has ended. The transformation remains. They are different consequences of the same decision."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "His death ended your relationship. It does not reverse what has already happened to your flesh."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You endured the consequences of the encounter. That does not mean you accepted the gift. We will talk about what happened to you without attributing someone else's decision to you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A Behelit. Where did you find it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then pause before going further. The changed stone has not yet changed you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Hearing a call does not mean answering it. Don't confuse the ability to open a door with the need to step through it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I remember what was said. Continue."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then make sure your actions show it. Your former body is no longer promised to you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The change has become visible. Others will now judge you before your first word."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have learned to use it. Learn its limits now, before an enemy forces you to do so in battle."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have become what you accepted the beginnings of in the circle. That does not make you equal to those who offered the gift."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your body has stopped changing. That does not free you from responsibility for how you use it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You destroyed the bearer of a power and chose to preserve it within yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Service does not end the moment a reward is received."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You refused to continue serving. But your earlier consent has already changed you. Don't expect the break to undo the past."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The master is gone. Your life remains. Don't waste it waiting for another."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You refused, knowing you would not leave unharmed. Now you must go on with the consequences of that choice."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You carry the possibility of an encounter whose consequences you do not yet know."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Possessing the stone is not consent. Don't give your answer before you understand the question."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "\"Fold them at the door, if you can. This is a forge, not a field.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "\"The straps will be harder to manage now. Don't tighten them blindly. First check where they restrict movement.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "\"I see ordinary armor won't fit you the way it used to.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "\"Your protection has become part of your body. Then you must treat it as a body, not as a suit of plate you can take off.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "\"Take your time. I'll try to understand. If it's hard, show me.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "\"I hear that speaking is difficult for you. You needn't hurry for my convenience.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "\"The bench might not hold. Better stand here, by the wall.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Show me what you found, or describe it. I'll try to remember."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A throwing knife's hilt was found beside the remains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A torn armor clasp was found beside the remains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A broken piece of scabbard was found beside the remains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A crushed sewing kit was found beside the remains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Judeau. He used to turn his knives over in his hand, even while talking. If a hilt like that was lying beside him... Thank you for telling me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me about him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Pippin. I repaired his equipment. He would bring a broken thing, wait quietly, and always help tidy up afterward."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Corkus. Always grumbling about scabbards, straps, the road. Now I even miss his grumbling."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Gaston. He knew how to work cloth, and talked about the business he would start after the war. Talks like that gave all of us hope."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You've returned. With results, I hope."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Beyond these walls lies chaos. People tear at one another for a handful of grain, a mouthful of water.\n\nHere, there is a master. Here, there is order. I need those capable of upholding it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&The Count raises his heavy body above the dungeon floor and bars your way.\n\n\"Enough. You stand before me instead of lying on the floor. So either you are worth something, or you have yet to understand where you are.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You raised your hand against what belongs to me.\n\nAnd came here again, as though you still had the right to ask for anything?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Branded one. You came to my house yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Empty-handed or bearing steel, you have entered my domain all the same."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The time to ask for a place at court has passed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm listening."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't need your permission."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've come to end your rule."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you demand?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I brought what you asked for."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm not finished yet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your help has worn off."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your help is still with me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will my new nature remain?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "End the conversation."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are you offering me service?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've made up my mind."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I am offering you an end to being a vagabond who can be kicked back onto the road.\n\nAccept my spark, and you will have a place in this house. A real one. Not charity."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What does serving you mean?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will you do to me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Who do you protect here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why me in particular?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What happened to your servants?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've decided."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "While you stand in my halls, you need far more than you imagine.\n\nI am still giving you a choice. Use it while I do."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Decide."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll accept your spark. I'll serve. Change me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to ask something else."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I will not be your subordinate."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll take your gift. Let's see who can use it better."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Come closer.\n\nNow you have a place.\n\nNow we can discuss your duties."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have not yet agreed. The decision remains yours."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Let's discuss my duties."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Back to my questions."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then your very presence has tested my patience long enough."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Defend yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You still stand here only because I permitted you to speak."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We'll see who is left standing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I will give your body what it could not gain in its whole miserable human life. You will endure more. Be capable of more."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And my former shape?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then why waste my time with empty words?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. Your nature is no longer what it was.\n\nDon't hope to shed it by forgetting your duties. It does not work that way."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Put it down.\n\nGood. I see you remember your place."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Strength demands loyalty. I never promised to feed you power forever for one fortunate decision in the past."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I remember my part of the bargain. While the aid lasts, no further delivery is required."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Well? What brings you here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Stay with the Dogs. Strength, plunder, fun. Not a life spent asking permission to pass.\n\nYou'll decide who gets past, and who gets buried."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Wyald bares his teeth, bracing his enormous limbs against the ground.\n\n\"Hey! Don't go soft on me yet. Got a question. Aren't you tired of shaking at every shadow on the road?\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Baring your teeth at me?\n\nAbout time we found out what they're really worth!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Come on, swordsman. Show me why you're here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Come on! Show me what your words are worth!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Depends on what you're offering."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm not afraid of you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Get out of my way."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What business?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And what's in it for you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Another fang for the pack. A good fang is always welcome."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you call strength?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What place will you give me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will happen to my appearance?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What about the weak?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will you demand?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why offer me this instead of just getting rid of me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Now that's a good start.\n\nLet's see how you finish."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm in your pack. Give me strength. I won't ask to go back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Keep your pack."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't need your handout. I'll take my share of power straight from your hands."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That's more like it!\n\nHa! Try staying on your feet first.\n\nThe Dogs are watching. Don't embarrass me already."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Finally. I thought you'd talk me to death."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Now I like you!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It'll stop being so flimsy. You'll see how much of it was useless. All that softness just getting in the way."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There'll be no going back?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then stop blocking my view."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Nope. You've got to live with it now.\n\nDon't like it? Get angry. Maybe that anger will be good for something."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yeah! Better already. Someone like that is worth talking to."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Want my help, do you?\n\nBring something worthwhile. I don't feed anyone for their pretty eyes."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're back! What's out there, beyond the trees?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You can stay here. You don't have to go back to them.\n\nThey only frighten you. Order you around. Hurt you, and then wonder why you don't trust them."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Wings flicker between the trees. Rosine hovers over the path, studying you.\n\n\"Are you from there? From the places where the houses are full of the dead?\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I let you in. You knew where we lived.\n\nAnd you still did this?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Have you come to destroy my home?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Stay away from us!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm looking for whoever lives in this valley."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What is happening here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I haven't found it yet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do I need to do to stay?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Become one of us. Then you'll understand how good it really is here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Who lives in the valley?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What does becoming one of you mean?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I be able to leave?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why do you want to keep me here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What if I don't like it here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What's inside the cocoons?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So will you stay?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll stay. I understand I won't return to being human. Change me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. I won't let you change me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll take your strength myself. From your flesh."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then don't be afraid. I'm here.\n\nThere. Now you're one of us."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then why did you come at all? To look at us? And then return with the others, and with fire?\n\nI heard you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're just like them.\n\nAt least you aren't pretending."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your body will be different. You'll stop seeing the valley through an outsider's eyes. Human eyes."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I still be myself?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then keep looking. You know where to find us. You won't forget the way."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're still one of us. That won't go away, whatever you're feeling now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes, that will do.\n\nStay close."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I can't keep going without meat for the nest. Bring some, and I'll help again."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "All right...\n\nJust don't say afterward that you weren't welcome here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Report."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have come far enough for me to consider you a warrior rather than a passing madman.\n\nI can offer you service. Strength to endure what breaks ordinary human limits."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Grunbeld turns his whole body toward you. His hammer stays lowered.\n\n\"Stop. One more step will mean you came to fight.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You broke your oath by your actions. Explanations will change nothing now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Raise your weapon. Your road onward goes through me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The conversation is over."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I will hear you out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You know why I've come."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Speak."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What is the assignment?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I failed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And submission to you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes.\n\nI do not give strength without obligations. It does not happen, and should not."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you require of a vassal?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What is the price of this armor?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What does the oath mean?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you forbid retreat?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why did you choose me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I saw you at Flora's home."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I accept service and swear to fulfill its terms. Give me a new nature."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I will not swear an oath to you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll take your strength after the battle. Without an oath."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your oath is heard.\n\nGrow accustomed to your strength.\n\nThen begin the work. Not before."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then what remains between us is the reason you came here armed.\n\nPrepare yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Win first."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It will become part of your being. It will give you endurance no ordinary steel forged by human hands can provide."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I be able to get rid of it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "State the reason.\n\nSet right what is within your power. And do not report success before it is achieved. That is worse than delay."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No.\n\nYour new nature will stay with you whatever happens. We are speaking of the aid I choose to give beyond that."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Present what you have brought.\n\nAccepted. You will receive the promised aid."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It must be renewed. You know the terms. I did not conceal them."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Carry out my will. Guard what is mine. Bring what I demand.\n\nAnd do not make me repeat myself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What if I disagree with your will?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then you should have remained beyond the gates."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You are asking to leave it behind yourself. Or did you expect to try on my gift like someone else's cloak, wear it for an evening, then return it?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They were given the chance to be more useful than before."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They don't all look pleased."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The contentment of servants is no measure of the strength of rule."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Those who serve me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is that what you call your prisoners too?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They are under my authority. Do not confuse the standing of a companion with that of someone dragged here in chains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Because you came here on your own feet. Most are escorted or dragged.\n\nLet us see if you have the sense to make use of that difference."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Take what you want. Hold it when someone comes to take it back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Even if I have to take what's someone else's?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're catching on fast. I like it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Find it yourself. Show your teeth, bring in spoils, and they'll notice. Don't worry."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And I'm the one in charge. Wouldn't even suggest testing that."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Want to go back, and you'll howl. Just a different kind of howling."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They hide. Run. Sometimes they're useful. Exactly as long as they're useful."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you abandon your own just as easily?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Keep up with the pack, and you won't have to find out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Plunder. Deeds. More noise from you in a fight than whining afterward.\n\nAnd when I call, you come. No arguing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Plenty of time to finish you off. Nothing hard about that.\n\nBut what if you turn out to be amusing? A shame to throw that away for nothing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Those who no longer have to go back there.\n\nThey have a different home here now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Did they want this themselves?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They wanted things to get better. And I helped. Those aren't the same thing, are they?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You came here because it hurt to be the way you are now, didn't you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That isn't what I asked."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I can't leave everything as it is and make it different at the same time. It doesn't work like that."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If I want to."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Everything beyond them is the same as before. Even if you leave, you won't become human again."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They change in there. First they need quiet. A little."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are they afraid?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Sometimes they're afraid. They still remember too much.\n\nThat will pass."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Because you're still listening. Usually they come with fire. Or with iron.\n\nYou could simply stay. That's rare."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You haven't even tried yet. And you already sound like them."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Carry out your orders. Protect what is entrusted to you. Answer the summons.\n\nDo not hide failure behind a lie. I will not forgive that."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What if an order disgusts me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Decide that before the oath, not afterward.\n\nI will hear an objection. But the decision remains mine. That is the order of things; otherwise service is meaningless."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No.\n\nThink about that now, before asking for such strength."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That your word can be relied on even when keeping it is hard. Especially then."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What if I leave?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Abandoning your duty does not become freedom merely because you call it that."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A needless death proves no endurance.\n\nA warrior may retreat to fight again. But one who abandons an entrusted line and the companions beside him answers for that choice himself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You stood before me with the chance to turn back, and did not.\n\nThat is enough for an offer. Respect will require more."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then you know I was carrying out an order."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That was a peaceful home. People could have stayed and lived there."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Have you come to demand an answer for that?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes. Defend yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to understand what serving you will cost."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've heard enough."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Including orders you would not have chosen yourself.\n\nNow you cannot say you did not understand that beforehand."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You know the decision will stay with you. What else do you wish to ask?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What else must you know?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Void does not blink. He seems to do nothing at all that would betray a living creature. The air around him feels thicker than elsewhere in the circle, and breathing near him is somehow harder.\n\n\"You seek a reason for your presence here.\n\nOr permission to accept what you came for?\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Only a heavy silence answers."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why did the stone bring me here?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What is this place?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can I refuse?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will remain of my former self?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to ask about the gift."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've decided to accept the gift."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to leave as a human."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to speak with the others."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Step away."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Listen."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Step away toward the others."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your answer has not yet been given."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Back again. Is there another question, or hope of a different answer to the old one?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Slan does not step back as you approach. Instead, she leans forward as if catching a scent. Her gaze travels over your face, your hands, the way you hold your body: appraising, almost hungry.\n\n\"You're still trembling.\n\nAnd yet you came closer. I like that, when the desire to live overcomes disgust.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why isn't a human body enough?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will happen to the pain?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why are you offering this to me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Go. I'm in no hurry."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Think.\n\nDesire won't disappear merely because you stop speaking of it aloud."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Or perhaps one that makes refusal easier?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Well, have you found an explanation that makes agreeing easier?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Ubik does not stand still like the others. He sways gently, as though the ground beneath him differs a little from everyone else's. His smile suggests he already knows your answer and finds it amusing.\n\n\"Here you are, then. Let's see what questions you brought along.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is what I'm seeing real?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why are you showing me this?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you know what I want?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are you trying to deceive me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Hear them out. I'm curious which words you'll like."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then nothing has happened yet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Conrad stands as though he has always been here: before the circle, before the path leading to it. When he is silent, it is hard to tell whether it is silence or a very slow speech that has not yet begun.\n\n\"You brought a living body here.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And I want to take it back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What happens if I leave as a human?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can I survive this unchanged?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you call a gift?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I still be able to die?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you change the mind too?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Hear them."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "(Conrad says nothing more. He simply becomes still again, as though the conversation had never happened.)"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are you ready to answer?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Femto does not stare at you as the others do. He seems to look through you, which is far more unsettling than any direct gaze. The air around him hangs motionless, as though it too dares not stir.\n\n\"You have arrived. Speak.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What does abandoning my former life give me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I be able to wield this power?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why do you need my choice?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I become one of you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've seen your image before."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The choice remains yours."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "(Femto does not answer. He simply becomes still again, gazing through space as though the conversation had never happened.)"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Those before whom your human life ceases to be your only possibility."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The stone came into your hands. Not by chance, yet at no one's bidding but your own.\n\nYou heard the call. Answered with action. Now you see where that succession of steps has led."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So everything was predetermined?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You ask this before speaking your answer.\n\nPerhaps it is easier to think the answer has already been given for you. That is easier."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I chose to come myself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I didn't know how it would end."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then do not deny your own part when you see what it has led to."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Now you are permitted to know enough to answer knowingly. There will be no greater knowledge, either before or after."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Here the human world touches what its senses cannot usually contain.\n\nYou did not arrive by a road you can retrace with the same steps."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I be able to return?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes.\n\nThe question is what you will return as."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You may. Then you will leave this place without the gift.\n\nBut the body and mind you brought have already touched something for which they were not made. That does not pass without a trace simply because you wish it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is that punishment for refusing?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No one promised you a safe return.\n\nRefusing the gift does not undo what you have already endured here, in this place."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You will remember making the decision. Your life before this moment will not disappear.\n\nBut the body you lived in will cease to be the unchanging measure of all else."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What if I change my mind later?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Change your mind, yes.\n\nRestore your former existence, no."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It bleeds. Freezes. Tires sooner than you want.\n\nYou ask it for one more step, and it cannot take it. Have you never wanted to make it obey, just once?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A body's weakness is no reason to abandon it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Perhaps not for you. That must be why you're still standing here arguing instead of leaving."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are you promising invulnerability?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want strength, not someone else's will."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. You will endure more, yes. But even flesh like that will learn what a wound is. Invulnerability does not exist, even here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then listen carefully before agreeing.\n\nWanting everything without changing the slightest bit is especially human. Almost endearing, to be honest."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Not all pain will vanish. Some things will become unfamiliar. At first you won't even know whether they're pain or something else.\n\nThe body will change. And you will have to learn to live in it again."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That sounds almost pleasant."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm curious how you'll greet something you could never feel before.\n\nYou can call it something else if that makes it easier."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You wanted to live badly enough to reach this place.\n\nBut it seems simply continuing to live no longer satisfies you. Otherwise, why seek this particular thing?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to survive."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to stop being afraid."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You know nothing about me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then tell me: how much of your former self will you give for one more morning? It isn't free, you understand."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Strength will give you new reasons for confidence, that's true.\n\nBut I don't promise it will take away every reason for fear. Fear is a tenacious thing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then don't let me choose the words for you. Say what you want yourself. I'm truly curious."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A living creature trying to reason about its own fate as though it were someone else's business.\n\nYet your heart is beating faster than usual right now. That isn't someone else's."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you enjoy this?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Would you prefer me not to care?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You accept what is offered here, in this circle. You do not choose a form to suit your taste, like a dress at a market.\n\nTalking to me will not change that, however long we speak."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You made it here. You were afraid along the way. Saved your skin as best you could.\n\nFor those feelings, you were already certain enough that this was real. A little late to ask, don't you think?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What about everything around us?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And rightly so.\n\nHere you should be careful of the habit of believing the first explanation you hear. It is rarely the last."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why should I believe you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And the memories?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Especially if you like it. Check pleasing explanations twice."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You chose before which memories to revisit and which to push away.\n\nHere, it is simply harder to look away from what you pushed aside."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You called your former life your choice. We merely let you linger on that thought longer than you intended."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So you understand what you're refusing and what you hope to gain.\n\nThough humans are very good at seeing only the convenient half of a picture. You're unlikely to be an exception."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why only the bad things?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So you found something to object to. Good. Remember the rest too, now that you've started."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We can guess.\n\nStrength. Continuing to live. Never being helpless again. Choose whichever word you like best."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to protect those beside me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want revenge."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't know myself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't owe you an explanation."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then one day you'll have to decide whom to protect from yourself.\n\nBut today, of course, that seems a question for the distant future. It always does."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A convenient goal. It lets you avoid thinking about how to live once it's achieved."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There's an answer humans give far less often than they should. Refreshing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You don't, that's true.\n\nBut you will explain it to yourself sooner or later. Everyone must."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are you afraid of hearing a lie? Or of hearing exactly what you've long wanted to hear?\n\n\"Enough answering with questions. Can the gift be undone?\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is the change truly irreversible?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. There's an unadorned answer for you, since you ask."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then listen."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You will return.\n\nYou will carry the consequences."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What exactly will change?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Senses. Sleep. Thoughts.\n\nWhat you are accustomed to relying on may change."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will my sight or hearing get worse?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "So there's no leaving unharmed?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Perhaps. Hearing may weaken, sight lose its sharpness. Tremors, anxiety, memories that give no peace. You will not know beforehand what will stay with you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do not count on it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You are already surviving it.\n\n\"You know what I mean.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to understand what I'm agreeing to."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Neither way out promises your former state. Neither of them."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flesh able to bear greater power.\n\nAnd life within that flesh."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will it happen at once?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It will begin here.\n\nContinue after your return."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then why accept?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That is your question.\n\nAnd your answer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You will have to live with the changes.\n\nDo not call that preserving everything that came before. That would be untrue."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The ability to act beyond what your former body allowed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If that is not enough, do not agree. The decision is yours, not mine."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You will have to use it. No one here will live the rest of your life for you. Neither I nor anyone else."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I decide whom to turn it against?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Choosing a goal does not mean being able to reach it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You are offered a change. You may name reasons. You may refuse to hear them.\n\nBut the answer must be yours, not someone else's."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You call that freedom?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Difficulty does not remove the need to decide. Quite the opposite."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You will receive a gift, but no place among us."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "How much power will I get, then?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Enough for your former measure of things to become too narrow.\n\nNot enough to ensure you never meet a power greater than your own."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You saw an image."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I destroyed it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And yet you stand before me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Ask before you give your answer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will I be able to choose my form?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will the changes continue on their own?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "When will they end?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will you demand someone's life?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What is the price of returning human?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. You accept the gift. You do not determine its shape."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes. What you accept will grow within you after your return.\n\nYou will not be asked to agree anew to every change. Once accepted, it will run its course."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "When the new body has finished becoming.\n\nIt will not return to its former shape, after the first day or the hundredth."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You may leave without the gift.\n\nBut do not demand that what you endured leave no trace. That does not happen, here or anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What exactly will happen to me?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your senses may dull. Your hands may shake. Memories and anxiety may rob you of peace. There is no knowing beforehand which traces you will carry."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You are not asked to name another life here.\n\nYou are offered a change to your own. Those are different things."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You accept a change without choosing its form. You will not be able to regain your former body."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I accept the gift. I understand I cannot regain my former body."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "First, there's something else I want to ask."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm not ready yet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You already know the consequences.\n\nDo you confirm your refusal?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then turn toward the life you intend to continue.\n\nThe circle slips from sight as though it had never been there. In its place is only memory, drawn unwillingly into the open.\n\nFragments of a former life surface one after another. Indistinct places. Unfinished thoughts. Decisions revisited again and again without finding peace. Faces emerge and fade before you can see them clearly.\n\nYour attention catches precisely on anything resembling weakness: a doubt never overcome. Fear that made you keep silent. A step never taken. Everything else seems deliberately pushed into darkness, beyond your sight.\n\nFor an instant a thought slips through: was everything before this truly so little?\n\nYet even within that thought, you can feel how insistently it is being steered toward that conclusion. Too insistently to be chance."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're showing only what suits you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It's still my life."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't want to go back to this."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Enough. Make it stop."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Ubik: So you remember other things too. Good.\n\nDecide with those in mind as well, not just what we slipped before you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to know what awaits me outside."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Void: Then confirm that you intend to continue it. In words, not thought."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Slan: You can still accept the gift. The door has not closed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&The images fade at once, as though switched off. The five figures stand before you again, motionless and patient, as though there had been no pause."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Void: You may leave without the gift.\n\nBut do not demand that what you endured leave no trace. That does not happen, here or anywhere else.\n\nConrad: Body and mind have already been altered by the very fact of being here. You will not feel every consequence at once. Some will appear later."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I refuse. Return me as a human."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've changed my mind. I want to accept the gift."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Conrad: Senses. Habits. Clarity of thought. All may become different.\n\nWe promise you no return to your former state. No one does."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I understand now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What still holds you back?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You don't even know yet what your flesh will become. No one offered to let you choose it beforehand."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If I agree with you, will I become like you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You can return. But you cannot recover everything you had before this place. Body and memory will keep something of what you endured."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Here you give up your former flesh. You are not asked for another's life."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You will have to live in what you become. Not only at the moment you wanted strength, but every day afterward."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You cling so tightly to what came before. Let us see what you are really holding on to.\n\nThe circle slips from sight as though it had never been there. In its place is only memory, drawn unwillingly into the open.\n\nFragments of a former life surface one after another. Indistinct places. Unfinished thoughts. Decisions revisited again and again without finding peace. Faces emerge and fade before you can see them clearly.\n\nYour attention catches precisely on anything resembling weakness: a doubt never overcome. Fear that made you keep silent. A step never taken. Everything else seems deliberately pushed into darkness, beyond your sight.\n\nFor an instant a thought slips through: was everything before this truly so little?\n\nYet even within that thought, you can feel how insistently it is being steered toward that conclusion. Too insistently to be chance."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "All right, let's understand what you're going to agree to."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. Not even if you circle all five of us and return to whichever answer you liked best."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You'll leave human. Just don't expect memory, hearing, sight and peace to be exactly as you remember them."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We are speaking of your life. Don't be so quick to put someone else's in its place."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Make sure you don't later call your own consent someone else's mistake. That would be... unbecoming."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Of course. Only let's not remember it too selectively, shall we?\n\nThe circle slips from sight as though it had never been there. In its place is only memory, drawn unwillingly into the open.\n\nFragments of a former life surface one after another. Indistinct places. Unfinished thoughts. Decisions revisited again and again without finding peace. Faces emerge and fade before you can see them clearly.\n\nYour attention catches precisely on anything resembling weakness: a doubt never overcome. Fear that made you keep silent. A step never taken. Everything else seems deliberately pushed into darkness, beyond your sight.\n\nFor an instant a thought slips through: was everything before this truly so little?\n\nYet even within that thought, you can feel how insistently it is being steered toward that conclusion. Too insistently to be chance."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The form is not chosen."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Hearing. Sight. Steadiness of hands. Memory and peace. Some of these will change."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your body. Your change."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There will be no way back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Remember.\n\nThe circle slips from sight as though it had never been there. In its place is only memory, drawn unwillingly into the open.\n\nFragments of a former life surface one after another. Indistinct places. Unfinished thoughts. Decisions revisited again and again without finding peace. Faces emerge and fade before you can see them clearly.\n\nYour attention catches precisely on anything resembling weakness: a doubt never overcome. Fear that made you keep silent. A step never taken. Everything else seems deliberately pushed into darkness, beyond your sight.\n\nFor an instant a thought slips through: was everything before this truly so little?\n\nYet even within that thought, you can feel how insistently it is being steered toward that conclusion. Too insistently to be chance."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You may accept the power. But its nature is not yours to decree."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Refusal will preserve your humanity. It will not undo what you endured."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What is required is your own decision."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Speak your answer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Look at what you are choosing.\n\nThe circle slips from sight as though it had never been there. In its place is only memory, drawn unwillingly into the open.\n\nFragments of a former life surface one after another. Indistinct places. Unfinished thoughts. Decisions revisited again and again without finding peace. Faces emerge and fade before you can see them clearly.\n\nYour attention catches precisely on anything resembling weakness: a doubt never overcome. Fear that made you keep silent. A step never taken. Everything else seems deliberately pushed into darkness, beyond your sight.\n\nFor an instant a thought slips through: was everything before this truly so little?\n\nYet even within that thought, you can feel how insistently it is being steered toward that conclusion. Too insistently to be chance."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You can read about what you accepted and endured in the travel reference book."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Close."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A smith named Godo works deep in the forest. He is said to take on heavy blades and weapons other masters turn away. A young craftsman familiar with crossbows and mechanisms lives with him.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo keeps his forge far from the towns. He understands what a blade is for, and dislikes wasting iron on decoration. If my weapon can still be saved, he will say so plainly.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There is a house with a forge in the forest. I have not yet learned who works here.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The forge, with its hearth and workspace, is downstairs. The living quarters are above. This is the craftsmen's home, not an abandoned storehouse.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I was allowed to use a resting place. Passages must be kept clear, and the owners' tools left where they belong.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "After the Eclipse, the Knight brought me here. I regained consciousness beneath this roof.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The forge has been damaged. I cannot consider my former shelter safe until I inspect what remains.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo worked at this forest forge. He took on heavy blades and weapons other masters refused.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo kept his forge far from the towns. He understood what a blade was for, and disliked wasting iron on decoration.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Back to the list"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Close the journal"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Oak with Entwined Roots"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "An enormous oak stands deep in the forest. Entangled roots conceal the earth around its trunk.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Someone searched among the roots for a stone with human features. Those who left this trail considered the find important enough to return for.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The roots divide the ground into narrow passages. Signs of someone's work end among fresh cuts. Before approaching the trunk, I should check the way back.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The stone was real. I took it from beneath the roots.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Cave of Echoes"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Broad galleries and narrow side tunnels branch underground. In the darkness, it is hard to judge how far the cave extends.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A scout left information about a staircase, a detour and an old support. The trail suggests they were looking here for a stone with a human face.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The ring of a stone pendant carries around corners. The creature deeper inside reacts to it. The sound may buy time if the way to the stairs is prepared beforehand.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A narrow tunnel connects to the gallery. A support obstructs the passage; its fastening can be reached from deeper within the cave.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Behelit was found among the underground traces. I will still have to find an ordinary way out.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Lost Expedition Camp"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "An abandoned camp stands among the trees, with tents and equipment belonging to people of this world.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The expedition studied an unusual find. Its records repeatedly mention dreams of a red face. A creature appeared near the tents after the sample was moved.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The wounded were moved into a separate tent. A sentry advised keeping to cover and avoiding the open ground in front of the creature. The last order was to evacuate the people and leave the equipment.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The sample was a Behelit. The expedition understood the danger too late.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Forest Chapel"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A chapel stands in the forest. An old road leads to its doors.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They used to take in travelers and the wounded. Later, the inhabitants moved an unusual stone behind the altar and began calling it a miracle.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The doors were closed to those seeking help. A whisper was taken for an answer to prayer. The traces at the altar show how the wait for a miracle ended.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There is a way around the chapel. The last notes advise looking for the living instead of returning for the stone.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The stone from the reliquary was a Behelit.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Forest Hollow"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The trail of missing travelers leads into a forest hollow. A creature that hunts people hides here. Before descending, I should examine the approaches and leave a way to retreat.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The creature is dead. Traces of the places it came from may remain among its remains.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The scrap I found describes a ruined foundation and a fissure in the ground. The trail leads to a separate breach.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Ashen Rift"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A wound has opened in the earth among ruined foundations. Ash lies along its edges, and a heavy pulse rises from below. This is a separate passage between worlds.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The guardian fell, but the pulse has not stopped. The passage itself still needs examining.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The wound has cooled and its pulse has faded. It is quieter here. The creatures that already entered this world have not disappeared.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Among the surviving markings are routes to the Count's residence, the Black Dogs' camp and the misty valley.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Brand remains with me.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Closing the passage has not changed what is happening to my body.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count's Residence"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Fortified Residence"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The trail led to a fortified house. The information I have calls it the Count's residence.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A fortified house behind an outer enclosure. I have not yet learned who rules it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Behind the outward order lie executions, imprisonment and servants whose bodies can no longer be called human.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "One of the prisoners described rooms he knew and a service passage. His knowledge concerns this house; he knows little of what happens beyond it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count is dead. His rule over this house has ended, but the traces bound to him still need attention.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The passage at the residence is closed. This gives the surrounding area a respite, not an end to the invasion.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I accepted the Count's protection. With new flesh came a place at his court. I have yet to experience for myself what he calls protection.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Black Dogs' Camp"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Military Camp"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The trail leads to the Black Dogs' camp. The information names their commander: Wyald.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A military camp stands among the trees. I have not yet learned whom its inhabitants obey.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Here they tally spoils, hold captives and carry out the commander's orders.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Military routines survived even among monsters. People were entered alongside rations and equipment, as though all belonged on the same inventory.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald is dead. His death does not undo what happened at the camp, but this master will lead no one else away.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I agreed to join the Black Dogs. Wyald promised strength and a life free of human prohibitions. My body changed at once.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The road leads into a misty valley. The information I received connects it with Rosine's name.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The road brought me to a misty valley. I have not yet learned who hides among its inhabitants.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Creatures called fairies circle above the flowers. The trails of missing people lead toward silk and enormous roots. This place's beauty tells me nothing certain about those who live here.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Bodies change inside the cocoons. Breaking a shell before it opens is not the same as saving whoever was once inside.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rosine is dead. The refuge she promised will take no new victims at her bidding. One victory cannot restore those already changed.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I accepted Rosine's offer to stay among her people. The new body came at once. Human speech grew harder, and the promised safety proved no substitute for a will of my own.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld's Fortress"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Fortress"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The information I received connects the fortress with Grunbeld.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Heavy fortifications enclose the inner courtyard. I have not yet learned whose orders are followed here.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld survived at the spirit tree. This trail may lead to another encounter with him.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld died at the spirit tree. The fortress still holds the consequences of his rule and the passage bound to it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "After the battle at the spirit tree, I lost sight of him. That is not enough to consider him dead.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld fell. The change of form prolonged his resistance, but now the battle is truly over.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The passage in the fortress is closed. The surrounding area has gained a respite.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I swore an oath to Grunbeld. He gave me a shell and a place among his warriors. With that protection came the demands of service.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "House by the Spirit Tree"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "House by the Great Tree"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The trail leads to a house beside an enormous tree. The information names a witch, Flora.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A lived-in house is joined to enormous roots. Its mistress has not yet introduced herself.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Living rooms connect to enormous roots. There is space here to read, work and rest. The shelter rests on the mistress's care as well as the tree's strength.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora allowed me to rest and take the prepared supplies. The other things in the house belong to its inhabitants.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora knows about armor that lets the body keep fighting at its wearer's expense.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The house is under attack. Its former defenses no longer hold back every enemy. The familiar passages are now ways out.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I escaped the house. Fire and battle remained behind me. What survived is still unknown.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The house by the spirit tree is lost. Fire passed through familiar rooms. This place can no longer be the refuge it was.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Living rooms were connected to enormous roots. There was space here to read, work and rest. The shelter rested on the mistress's care as well as the tree's strength.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora spoke of armor that lets the body keep fighting at its wearer's expense.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My Shelter"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I chose a place to return to from the road. Water, dressings and a clear way out should always remain here.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A sign of stones and bones stands near my sleeping place. It restrains the Brand's nighttime call nearby, but does not stop creatures already here.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My former shelter is no longer fit for rest. I will need to find another.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo owns the forest forge. He speaks sharply and gets down to business quickly. First he wants to see the weapon, then hear requests about it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo recognized me. He still grumbles about my blades and doesn't mince words. He judges iron more confidently than others judge people.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "His work is blades, iron fittings and repairs. He leaves mechanisms and crossbows to Rickert.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He took me in when I could not cross the threshold on my own. He asked no payment for water or a place by the wall.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "At the forge, Godo spoke of fire and sparks. A bright flash soon dies; work and those you care for remain. What matters is not only the strength of a blow, but the life you intend to return to.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I chose not to listen to his talk by the forge.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo refused to make this blade for me. He knows of the power I accepted, and believes I must now answer for my choice.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo owned the forest forge. He spoke sharply and got down to business quickly. First he wanted to see the weapon, then hear requests about it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo recognized me. He grumbled about my blades and didn't mince words. He judged iron more confidently than others judged people.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "His work was blades, iron fittings and repairs. He left mechanisms and crossbows to Rickert.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo refused to make this blade for me. He knew of the power I accepted, and believed I must now answer for my choice.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo is dead.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert works alongside Godo. He understands crossbows, triggers and fastenings. He can spend a long time on a small part if a weapon's reliability depends on it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He traveled with the Band of the Hawk. In battle, he relies on a crossbow, position and preparation more than on the force of a sword stroke.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert helped me after my rescue. He did not know what had happened inside the Eclipse.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I told him what I saw in the Eclipse. He learned of Griffith's betrayal and the deaths of his comrades.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I told Rickert the band died in an attack by men and beasts. I kept Griffith's betrayal from him.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I have not yet told him what I endured. He is left with questions about his comrades' fate.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I admitted that I had lied. Rickert now knows the truth and remembers my deception. One admission is not enough to make everything as it was.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Trust has become possible between us again. That has not erased our earlier conversation from memory.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert decided to travel with me. He agreed to be a companion, not someone's property.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "After what I said, Rickert refused to travel with me. Ordinary work at the forge remained a separate matter.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert worked alongside Godo. He understood crossbows, triggers and fastenings. He could spend a long time on a small part if a weapon's reliability depended on it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He traveled with the Band of the Hawk. In battle, he relied on a crossbow, position and preparation more than on the force of a sword stroke.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert is dead.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A rider whose helmet resembles a skull. He found a passage out of the place of sacrifice and carried me through.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He said he had an opportunity to intervene and took it. He demanded no new debt for the life he saved.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He has long fought beings from beyond. He gave neither his name nor his history.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Knight continued on his way. He warned me not to expect him to wait at this threshold again.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora is a witch who lives by the spirit tree. She speaks calmly and does not promise deliverance from every misfortune. For her, knowledge is bound to care for the living.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "She explained that the Brand connects its bearer to another side of the world. Simply defeating one monster does not sever that bond.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora knows the price of the Berserker Armor. It can force the body to keep fighting when an ordinary person could no longer stand.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "She allowed me to take the prepared aid. It is a gift from the mistress of the house, not permission to empty it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora learned of my change. She did not promise to restore my former body. Discussing how to use the will I still have proved more important than a promise of easy healing.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora was a witch who lived by the spirit tree. She spoke calmly and did not promise deliverance from every misfortune. For her, knowledge was bound to care for the living.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora knew the price of the Berserker Armor. It can force the body to keep fighting when an ordinary person could no longer stand.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora is dead.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Prisoner of the Residence"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A man held in the Count's residence. He knows the servants' habits and some of the service rooms. He fears the master and doubts that outside help is even possible.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He told me what he could about a way through the house. His help made it clearer where the servants could be bypassed.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count's hold over him is ended. What he will do with that freedom is not yet known.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A man held in the Count's residence. He knew the servants' habits and some of the service rooms. He feared the master and doubted that outside help was even possible.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The prisoner is dead.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Work at the Forest Forge"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Work here is paid for with usable metal and other needed materials. Godo handles blades; Rickert handles mechanisms and bolts. It is worth discussing an agreement before bringing random scrap.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Materials go to the craftsman who accepted the job. Finished work takes time. When it is done, I must return to the forge to collect it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Blade Repairs"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo will not reforge a sound blade without need. First he examines the edge and says whether work is required. If the damage is serious, it will take materials and time at the forge.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I must leave the blade itself for repair. While the smith has it, I will need another weapon on the road. Once the work is finished, I will get my blade back.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Great Blades"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A long fighting blade without ornament. Such a sword needs reliable tempering and good balance. Size alone does not make good work.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My homemade blade follows the general design, but it is heavier, rougher and less durable in use. This is my attempt, not Godo's work.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Godo made a blade for an impossible task: killing a dragon. An ordinary warrior can barely lift this iron. The smith does not speak of it as a handsome parade weapon.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Prosthesis and Arm Cannon"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert can assemble a mechanical replacement for a lost hand. The device combines a moving mechanism with a concealed cannon. The work requires precise fastenings as well as iron.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The device is finished, but has not yet become part of my arm. Before relying on it in battle, I must fit it and check the mechanism.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The prosthesis is fitted to my arm. I must get used to its weight and movement, and keep the cannon working and loaded with suitable charges.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I assembled this mechanism myself.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I assembled it after losing my hand. Rickert remarked on that work in particular.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert explained how to assemble a mechanical replacement for a lost hand. The device combines a moving mechanism with a concealed cannon. The work requires precise fastenings as well as iron.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Crossbow and Bolts"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rickert values a reliable trigger more than a showy modification. A crossbow helps keep distance, but requires a suitable position and time to reload.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I can commission bolts from him by supplying the materials. Discussing bolts does not oblige me to order a prosthesis or invite Rickert on the road.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Stone with a Human Face"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A small stone with human features. It is hard to mistake it for an ordinary trinket.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The accounts of those who held it before repeatedly mention whispers and the feeling of a foreign call.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Now I too have heard the call. It speaks to a desire that is difficult to say aloud.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Desecrated Behelit"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Blood changed the stone. The call grew more insistent. It promises a different way out of the ceremony, but no return to my former life.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I was warned: the passage is dangerous even to one who refuses the offered power. Changes may remain forever.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I passed through a place of sacrifice. The band I knew before that night was among the doomed. Griffith stood on the other side of what happened.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Beyond the passage lay a place of sacrifice. People and traces of a last resistance lay among the creatures. Their past was not mine, but what I saw has become part of my life.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Skull Knight carried me out. The ceremony stayed behind; its consequences stayed with me.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That night, I lost my left hand.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "That night, I lost an eye.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I managed to destroy the form holding the scene together. That was not the destruction of the entire God Hand.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Ceremonial Circle"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Five figures waited at the end of the path. They spoke of fate, desires and choice. The offered gift did not promise to preserve my former body.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I could accept the gift, but could not decree the form it would give me.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I agreed. The participants in the ceremony returned me outside. Now the change continues within me.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I refused even after the final warning. They returned me without the gift. The human body did not endure that passage without consequences.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Those Who Stood at the Circle"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Void spoke of causality and a decision that cannot be undone. The stone brought me to a choice, but did not make its consequences someone else's responsibility.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Slan spoke of the desire to live and a body able to receive more than a human could. In her promises, flesh and passion sounded like a single price.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Ubik turned to memory and to how easily a person explains their own desire to themselves. His words made me doubt not only what I saw, but my own excuses.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Conrad spoke little. In his answers, human vulnerability seemed part of inevitable decay. He promised no departure from this place without consequences.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Femto spoke as though the former human measure no longer mattered. The strength he offered did not make its recipient equal to the one offering it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Trace of Refusal"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I returned human. Refusal left me no accepted power, but the ceremony still changed how I hear, see or experience my surroundings.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Some sounds have grown muffled. I have to listen closely to hear familiar things.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My sight is no longer what it was before the passage.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A tremor that was not there before has entered precise movements.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Memories return uninvited. Sometimes the present briefly loses its hold before them.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The sense of danger remains even where I cannot yet see anything.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Brand remains the mark of a sacrifice. Beings beyond the boundary see it where human eyes see nothing. Night eases their way to the marked.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Pain and blood may warn of a nearby creature. The warning does not name the enemy or reveal a safe road.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Closing one passage does not sever the Brand's bond.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Night Pursuers"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Silence does not mean the trail is lost. I should prepare a resting place before dark and keep essential things near the exit.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A door will not stop every creature. The protection of walls must not leave me without a way to retreat.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Dawn does not destroy creatures that already arrived. Before stepping outside, I must look for those still there.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Sign of Stone and Bone"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A small sign of stones and bones restrains the Brand's nighttime call nearby. It does not destroy creatures or replace walls, water and a way out.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The sign requires eight stones and four bones. It is built on clear ground near a sleeping place.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The bed should remain near the sign and on the same floor. The sign works under open sky too, but that does not make an open clearing a reliable shelter.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wounds Between Worlds"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The boundary between worlds is damaged. Creatures that did not belong to these lands before arrive through separate passages.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Defeating the creature holding a passage does not always close the wound itself. After the battle, I must examine what it left.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A closed passage gives the surrounding area a respite. Creatures already here remain, and distant wounds still exist.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Reflections"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Not every familiar shape belongs to the being itself. Reflections bearing part of another's power arise at the boundaries between worlds.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The reflection of Griffith I defeated was not the original. The disappearance of its shape does not prove the death of the one whose image it took.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The stone I found was real, though the creature around it was a reflection.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Judeau"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Among the traces of the last battle, I recognized Judeau. Even there, he tried to buy others time. He deserves to be remembered for more than that last night.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I found evidence of Judeau. The traces suggest he tried to help others escape the crush. Before that night he had a life I know only in fragments.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The hilt of his knife survived.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Knight said that keeping a person's memory means remembering how they lived, not only how they died.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Pippin"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Pippin held the passage to the end. Others could still get away behind the place where he stood.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The traces by Pippin's body show resistance in a narrow passage. He stayed between the creatures and those still trying to escape.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A broken clasp survived among the fragments.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Not every deed can be measured by who remains standing after the battle.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Corkus"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Corkus wanted to escape war and mud. We often disagreed, but that does not diminish what was taken from him.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The evidence of Corkus holds ordinary human hopes. Monsters cut them short just as they did the dreams of those called heroes.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A piece of his scabbard survived.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No one has to become a hero to deserve a life.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Gaston"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Gaston wanted to leave war behind one day and live by his own work. His future was quieter than others' dreams of a kingdom, but meant no less to him.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I found the trace of a man named Gaston. He hoped for an ordinary life after the war. Such hopes are easily lost amid great names and banners.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "His sewing tools recall the life he wanted to return to.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Berserker Armor"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "This armor lets the wearer fight beyond ordinary pain. It does not leave the body unharmed or cancel the price of wounds already received.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Obtaining the armor does not mean learning to resist it. The power holding a body in battle can destroy its wearer.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I already have the complete armor. I need understanding and control, not a second set.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I have part of the armor. It is not yet a complete set.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora refused to give me new armor after my choice. She knows of the power I accepted.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Fire at the Spirit Tree"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I escaped, but the house by the spirit tree is lost. Beyond its familiar doors lie rooms where, only recently, one could rest and talk.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Closed wounds brought a local respite. They did not stop the worlds colliding. The road continues among consequences that can still be changed.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The trail leads to Grunbeld's fortress.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld is dead. The fortress still holds the passage bound to him and the consequences of his rule.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I do not know what became of Grunbeld after the battle.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Respite"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The wounds whose trails I followed are closed. Those places have grown quieter. This is not the end of darkness, but people have gained time they did not have before.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The known roads of this journey are traveled. Not every decision was a victory: an accepted pact left its trace too. Where breaches closed, the surrounding areas gained a respite. Other wounds and creatures already here have not disappeared.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Brand remains. The next night still requires preparation.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The power I accepted remains with me. A finished hunt does not restore a former body.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I remained human and carry the consequences of that passage.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My Body"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I have already agreed. I feel the change, but do not yet know its final shape. No one offered to let me return for another share of power.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The change continues on its own. New sensations and needs do not appear at once. The body's greater endurance does not mean it has stopped being wounded.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I took the flesh of a defeated creature into myself. It did not remain ordinary food. Now its strength is changing my body.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "This choice leads no way back. Accepting different flesh in place of the first does not undo what has already happened.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Bone emerged beneath the scar, tendons stretched and fingers straightened. My left hand grew back. This came with the accepted change, not ordinary healing.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The cannon mechanism stayed on my forearm. The new hand did not destroy the device already fitted there.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My body lengthened and my fingers changed. Distance sometimes feels unlike what the eye sees. A short step can carry me through a gap I once would have crossed another way.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A bend in space can soften a blow, but the flesh itself is not invulnerable. Ordinary rigid gloves no longer fit my hands.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My flesh has grown stronger and more supple. I can draw from it a weapon I did not have before. Regaining strength costs hunger and time.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rigid equipment on my hands obstructs the changed body. The ability to recover is no reason to forget wounds and food.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My silhouette has become harder to hold in view. I can turn another's attention toward a false target and briefly disrupt an enemy's perception.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "This promises no mastery over every mind. Ordinary rigid helmets and masks do not fit my changed head.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My flesh has grown thicker and heavier. My touch corrodes living bodies, and my breath leaves a caustic haze. My own strength demands care near those I do not want to hurt.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I move more slowly. Ordinary rigid armor for the torso and legs does not fit my new body. A cloud is not safe merely because I released it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Dark wings changed my back and balance. My movement is swifter. With pressure, I can push an opponent back and disrupt their advance.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The wings need room. Ordinary torso clothing obstructs them; this strength has not given me endless flight.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My body has grown heavy and pliable. The changed flesh endures more, and its tendril can reach an enemy within striking distance.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Durability costs slowness. Rigid armor constricts my torso and arms. Recovery remains a bodily need, not proof of immortality.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The new body strains toward a lunge and a grasp. Close combat has become more natural; precise work, harder.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "After exertion, strength returns more slowly. My changed hands and feet do not fit ordinary rigid gloves and footwear.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Insectlike wings unfolded behind my back. They help me move quickly and soften a fall, if my body and burden allow their use.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I have not gained free ascent into the sky. Heavy and tight equipment obstructs my wings, and my body's fragility has not vanished.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A heavy carapace closed over my body. Heat has become easier to endure, and my breath can become flame.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My body needs more food and recovers from exertion more slowly. Rigid armor will not fit over the shell. Resistance to heat does not make every fire safe.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count called me his. My body grew denser and slower, and a tendril grew from it. The new protection is bound to the one who gave it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My changed torso will not fit ordinary rigid armor. I accepted a place at another's court, but must still answer for my own actions.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald gave me a beast's body. It strains forward toward a short rush and a blow. Crude strength costs clumsiness at precise work.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rigid gloves do not fit my changed hands. His approval is no substitute for rest after battle.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rosine accepted me among her people. My head and hands changed; words grew harder. I can still choose and act.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My former human work takes more effort. Ordinary rigid helmets, masks and gloves do not fit this body.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The oath I accepted left a shell on my body. It withstands some blows and heat, but makes movement heavier.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Ordinary rigid armor constricts my torso and arms. Beneath the master's protection remain the demands of service.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "My bond with the master no longer gives its former support. The changed body remains. A broken oath did not make me human again.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The master is dead. With him, the support ended, but the flesh I accepted from him has not vanished.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The rebuilding is finished. My body has taken its new shape. Now I must live with it, not wait for another night to restore my former self.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count is dead. He will give no more orders or offer a helping hand. There is no one left to offer one.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The body you received from him has not gone away. It is yours now, truly yours, with no master behind your back.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald is dead. His voice will no longer summon the pack. It is probably already prowling on its own, without a leader.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What he gave you remains yours. The death of the one who changed you does not undo the change.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rosine is gone. You must now make sense of the home she promised with your own mind, without her voice behind your shoulder.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Your human body has not returned. And it will not.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld is dead. There will be no new orders. No one is left to give them.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The shell he gave remains part of your flesh, just as before.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A heavy seal left by the Count. Worn, it helps strike beings from beyond the boundary. Its power is not directed against every living body.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Beast's Knot"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A sinewy knot sharpens the sense of what moves in darkness. With it, the night road is easier to make out.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Veil of the Misty Valley"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A thin veil retains a trace of the strange valley. Worn, it helps evade a blow, but promises no escape from every attack.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Shard of the Fiery Carapace"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The shard belongs to the apostle itself. Worn, it helps endure heat, but does not protect against smoke or make fire safe.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It cannot be confused with the charred clasps of the garrison's people.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Order from the Plundered Caravan"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The wheel broke before dusk. The iron fastenings were left beneath the iron-bound chest; the grain was taken.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "An order is tucked between the pages: \"Take the bent blades to Godo's forest forge. A young crossbow maker works with him. Follow the old cart tracks through the woods.\"\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Turns and crossings are marked in the margins.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Scout's Note"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Something watches the open clearing. I saw trees move without wind. I tied my pack above the washout and took the lower path to check the other bank. If I don't return, keep to the rocks and leave enough room to turn back.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Letter from the Wayside Camp"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We're leaving before the next dusk. The water is clean; those who follow may need the blanket more than we do.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The smith Godo repaired our broken blade. His young helper makes crossbow bolts. We wrote down the return route here: the old path, the stream crossing, then the charcoal burners' trail. It's a long walk, but there's a craftsman at the end of the road.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora's Advice for the Road"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Clean cloth for dressings must be boiled. A waterskin is best sewn before a long journey. Drinking water, a sleeping place and a clear exit matter more than a comfortable room.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A small sign of stone and bone helps restrain the nighttime call, but does not drive away a creature already standing at the door.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rescued Manuscript"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora compares the joined worlds to roots grown together across a wound. A quiet place can shelter a traveler; one refuge cannot heal the whole world.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Traces of smoke remain in the margins. Most of the research lay beyond the torn pages.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Leaf-Shaped Bookmark"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A wooden bookmark shaped like a leaf survived in a stone niche among the roots. Carved into it are the words: \"Leave a light for the next traveler.\"\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Charred Scrap"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Between the charred edges are a broken road, a ruined foundation and markings around a fissure. The creature from the hollow carried this route to another breach.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Broken Root Cutter"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Fresh cuts end midway through the roots. Two rows of notches are carved into the handle; one stops abruptly. These people tried to cut a path to the stone face, not fight what lived beneath it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Two Travelers' Charm"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The inscription names two travelers and asks that both return home. The second knot was tied by a trembling hand. On the bark nearby is a dark stain like the one on the discarded root cutter.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Last Note at the Oak"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We left the cart on the old path. The face is caught in the roots, just as he said. While the creature circled the trunk, I waited behind the thick roots and didn't move.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We'll return by the old western path. If only one of us reaches the cart, leave the other's name on the cord.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora's Herbal"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Dry the herbs separately. Boil clean cloth for wounds. Mend old sleeves before the next journey. Keep both passages around the spirit tree clear.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A refuge remains a refuge because someone cares for it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Cave Scout's Sketch"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I marked the broad gallery to the east. Beneath it, a narrow tunnel skirts the rock and joins the gallery twice. In the western hall we heard the pendant before we saw what followed its sound. The bends hid us from its eyes.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There is a passage with a support near the stairs, but the peg faces deeper into the cave. If we make it, I'll leave another mark by the broken prop.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Chapel Aid List"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Water was stored in the eastern room, blankets and dressings in the vestry. An early entry mentions a traveler with a repaired sword and bolts: \"Godo's forge is still working in the forest. The old man and his young helper take usable metal in payment.\" He drew the road on the back.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Later, instead of food portions, they began counting hours beside the red stone. The last volunteer wrote: \"This was meant to be a refuge.\"\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Keeper's Confession"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We called the stone a miracle because we needed a miracle. We moved it behind the altar and stopped opening the door to strangers. When the whispering began, we decided we had been answered.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The handprints on the altar were not left during prayer.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A Refugee's Forest Road"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If the chapel is lost, leave through the breach in the western wall. An old rut farther into the forest leads to a great oak with tangled roots. Travelers spoke of another stone face. I have not seen it myself.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Sample Extraction Canceled"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The extraction order is crossed out.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Three of us described the same red face after spending the night here. When we moved the sample, scratching began behind the new tent. Pavel is wounded: the creature caught him when he stepped into the open. Cancel sample collection. Send transport for the wounded. We are leaving the equipment.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Last Words on Cloth"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We broke shields to build a wall. Held the passage until the wounded were carried through. There is no road back. Don't lose sight of the pale path. Enormous ribs lean toward the gathering place.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Prisoner List"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The names recur on execution notices. Shoes and cloaks were sorted before sentencing, as though their owner had already ceased to be a person. One entry was crossed out and replaced with \"sent below.\"\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Behind every neat column was a person they had already decided was a thing.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Physician's Notes"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The first pages concern boiled linen and ordinary wounds. Then sketches appear of a second mouth growing from a servant's chest.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The author stopped calling it a disease. Pieces of the master's flesh implanted another life in the victim. Familiar treatments did not restore the person.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Theresia's Ribbon"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The ribbon lay beside sewing and a book kept free of dust. A note calls the room Theresia's and forbids the servants to disturb it.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The same ruler who signed the prison lists protected this little island of ordinary life. It does not say where his daughter is now.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Two Roads from the Residence"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Two roads are marked on the map. One bears the Black Dogs' camp and Wyald's name; the other, a misty valley and Rosine's. Notes about missing caravans and closed roads run along the edge.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Black Dogs' Lists"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The lists separate soldiers, prisoners and those taken to the commander. The first pages record boot sizes and rations. Later notes describe distorted guards wearing the same uniforms.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Another life of the camp shows through the familiar military ledger.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Account of an Escape"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I hid this before roll call. The cage doors are tied, not locked with iron keys. Untie them from either side and pass through. The route through the quarry is longer, but open.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "At the bottom, a short word has been added beside one name: \"escaped.\"\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Commander's Orders"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald ordered the plundered supplies counted and a space cleared for fighting. Wooden barriers were dragged to the edges. Between the lines about spoils and people, one demand recurs: no one leaves without his permission.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The last sheet speaks of a fractured world. The crossing changed the commander's former fate. The one living in this camp is the man himself, not his reflection.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Valley Seeker's Account"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They called the winged things fairies because the flowers were beautiful. I followed a trail of abandoned shoes, past the games, toward the silk.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "In the quiet shells, no hope remained. In the moving ones was something already changed. I cannot bring them back. The western ravine offers a way around the grove to the enormous roots.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Faded Ribbon"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The ribbon was tied to a branch as a marker for a game. Farther on, the same knot is caught in a split shell. The flowers kept growing after the games stopped.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Sometimes all a person leaves is a thing easily walked past.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Sentry's Message"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Mikhail, if you reach the camp first: we moved the wounded to the southwest tent. The creature came out of the northern tent and caught Pavel in the open. Keep behind the tent walls and leave through the gap in the eastern fence. We are leaving before dusk.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Lena.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Last Vigil"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The last prayer is crossed out.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We barred the main doors to keep strangers out. Now footsteps sound inside. Irina carried the remaining blankets through the vestry; I couldn't persuade her to return for the stone. The western wall is breached. Follow the living while there is still time.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Note on a Sleeve"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The eastern passage is wide enough to carry him, but the scratches there are fresh. I left the iron crowbar by the broken support. We circled the stone pendant and approached the prop from below. The peg can be pulled out from that side.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If he wakes, first we'll try to reach the stairs, not the red face.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Garrison Banner Clasp"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A charred clasp is all that remains of the garrison banner. Names of the people who held the southern road are scratched on the back.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "This is a human possession. The apostle's fiery shell did not belong to those whose names remain here.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Travel Journal\n\nRoads, faces and events. What I managed to learn and keep in memory."
msgstr ""

