#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "&Travel Journal"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Good to see you again. Outside, not through the bars."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It's your voice. I recognize your voice.\n\nBut what happened to you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I hear you. Just... stay a little farther away for now, all right?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Still can't get used to this quiet. Feels strange."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm still here. Haven't gone anywhere. How's the road?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're back. Learn anything?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Stay back. Please, stay back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Quiet... I got out of the cell, but I still have to reach the gates. Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I see you've opened it already. What now? It's still a long way to the gates, and not a straight one."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Quiet... keep it down.\n\nYou're not one of the ones bringing food. So who are you? What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't serve the Count."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm looking for the master of this place."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to get you out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Answer a couple of questions first."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm not going to hurt you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I need information about the house."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I can open the cage."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're right to be afraid."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "It's a long story."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm still the one who opened the door for you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm still the one you spoke to."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm stronger than the Count now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Who are you, then?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you know about the residence?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell me about the Count."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is everyone serving here like him?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Will you help me find a way around?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will it take to get you out?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count is dead."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I fought him, but I don't know how it ended."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What will you do now?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You're free. Why aren't you happy?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you owe me anything?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Let's discuss the way onward."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I should be going."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then don't stand rooted in the passage. If they notice, I'll have to explain who I was whispering with."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I won't ask why.\n\nJust understand: he's not human. Remember that. Not human."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "And I want to believe you. I really do.\n\nFirst, have a look at how this damned thing opens. Then I'll know whether you're all talk."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll see how I can help."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Go ahead. Just quietly. Sound travels far here, and not always in the direction you want."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Hauled supplies. Sacks, barrels, whatever they told me. Sometimes stayed in the storerooms to unload, helped with little things.\n\nKnew which door to knock on. Who to give the sacks to, who not to speak to at all. Thought that was enough to do my job in peace and go home.\n\nIt wasn't."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why did they lock you up?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What did you see?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Why didn't you try to escape?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do you have somewhere to go?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Heard a scream. Behind a door we'd been strictly told to stay away from.\n\nDidn't leave right away. Stood there. That was enough. They noticed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Just for that?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Nobody read me any charges, don't you worry. Hit me a few times, stripped me of everything, dragged me here. End of the conversation.\n\nIf you want to know exactly why, ask them yourself. Me, I'd rather never speak to them again. Ever."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Not as much as it feels like at night, when I'm trying to sleep.\n\nSaw them take a man in there. Later they brought his clothes out. Empty.\n\nNever saw him again. Don't know what happened to him. I won't lie and say I do."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I tried. Shook the bars until I heard footsteps. Stopped.\n\nThen started again. And stopped again.\n\nThere's plenty of time here. More than enough for starting over."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Away from here. I'll decide exactly where once I'm outside and can think a little instead of just shaking."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I know the service areas well. Where supplies went, where tools were kept, which passage the servants used to avoid the main rooms.\n\nI wasn't invited into the private chambers. That wasn't my road."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Where should I look for the Count?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "How can I get through less conspicuously?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Where can I find something useful?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Are there other prisoners?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He usually held court in the execution hall, to the northeast. Stairs lead down from there. But where he is now, I can't see from here, as you understand."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There's a pantry in the southwest kitchen. They kept bread, dried meat and water for the house there.\n\nUnless they've carried it all off since. I haven't been there in a long time."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There were others here, yes. How many remain now, I don't know. Can't see or hear much from here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you want to know?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Have you seen what he can do?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Has he always been like this?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Does he have a weakness?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've beaten things like him before."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "His story ends today."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've seen enough not to mistake you for a savior just because you came here.\n\nThere was a man who broke some rule, I don't know which. The Count took him... so easily. Like tossing an empty sack off his shoulder.\n\nI stopped watching after that."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I never knew him any other way. The way I fear him is the way I remember him.\n\nAsk someone who knew him better what he used to be. By this place's standards, I've barely arrived."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Even if I knew, I couldn't swear I'd have the nerve to use it.\n\nI won't lie just to get you to open my door. I don't know the weaknesses of things like him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then maybe you really understand where you've wandered.\n\nI don't. I know one thing: I want to get out. Alive."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Keep your voice down! Don't shout that from my corridor. All I need is for them to hear and decide who I've been conspiring with."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't know. I really don't.\n\nSome hit me for no reason, out of boredom maybe. Others looked away, pretended I wasn't there. And one... one left a little more water than he was supposed to. Quietly. Never said a word.\n\nI can't tell you what's under each one's skin. I don't know."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Can any of them be reasoned with?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Do they know what the Count does?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "How do they move around the house?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "No. I won't give you names just because someone didn't hit me once.\n\nHere a man can pity you and still call the guards as soon as your back is turned. It's that kind of place. I've been burned once already. I don't want a second time."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Some probably know. Others try as hard as they can not to. Easier to live that way.\n\nThey carry supplies. Lock doors. Wash floors as though nothing's wrong. The house goes on living as though none of it were happening."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They used to go through the west-wing records office and the narrow passage to the hall. I've learned by the footsteps when someone's coming this way.\n\nBut that's all I hear. Can't make out the whole house from here: who's standing where now, or when the guards change."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Good. One less obstacle. That's something."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A narrow service passage leads from the west-wing records office to the execution hall. A grille blocks it. You can go through the courtyard instead if you don't want to bother with the lock."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Where should I look for the key?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Is it safe there?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've already been through. The door is open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't need that detour."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I don't have a key. The scribe hid the service key in his chest, in the northern room of the west wing. It opened this grille and the passage to the hall.\n\nI saw where he put it myself. Whether anyone's checked since, I have no idea."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Less open ground, yes. Safe now? Couldn't say. The last time I used it was before they dragged me here. A lot could have changed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "As you wish. I told you about the road I used myself. That's all I have to offer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Good. One less obstacle. That's something.\n\nWhat's farther on? What's happening along the way?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "But I'll stand here for now. Sorry if you thought I'd dash straight for the gates. My legs aren't what they were, nor my head."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "First, open the door. That's one.\n\nTwo: make sure they don't grab me ten steps beyond it. That's happened before. Don't fancy doing it again."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll look for the key."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wait here. I'll check the way."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Follow me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Decide for yourself from here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "All right. I'll listen for what's happening out there."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Lead on. Tell me to stop, I'll stop. Won't argue. Not in any state for that."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Let's go."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm deciding already. That's why I'm standing here instead of running headlong."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then run when you're ready."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Did you see it yourself? You didn't just wound him and run before he recovered?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He won't get up again."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You killed him.\n\nThank you. Really. But I still feel... uneasy with you nearby. I'm sorry."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "How many times I imagined those words...\n\nAnd I'm still waiting for footsteps. A habit like that won't fade quickly, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll help you get out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'm not asking you to stay."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then I won't believe it's over yet either. Too early to celebrate."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Find water. Eat somewhere I don't have to wait for someone to open the door.\n\nThe rest, I'll decide later. For now, that alone will be happiness enough."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Maybe I haven't learned how yet.\n\nGive me a little time. I'm not used to the door behind me staying open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I've got almost nothing on me. If you wanted payment, you've come to the wrong man."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then stand where you are. I can hear you from there, perfectly well. You needn't come closer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll answer. Ask, just... just don't stand in the doorway, all right?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Open it. Open it, yes.\n\nJust don't ask me to follow you right away. Not now. Give me a little time to get used to who let me out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "What is it you want?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "All right. Not now, don't tell me.\n\nJust say why you came back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I remember. I really do.\n\nJust give me a little time to get used to seeing you like this. It's... not easy."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "One master like that was enough for a lifetime.\n\nI'm not looking for another. Not even one like you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Then thank you for that too."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Take care of yourself.\n\nI know how foolish that sounds, saying it to you after everything you did in there. Still. Take care."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I'll wait. Until I can walk out on my own, I'll wait here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If you come back this way... look in. Don't forget me here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I wasn't invited into the private chambers. That wasn't my road."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The man raises his head at the sound of footsteps."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to talk."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Open the grille with the service key?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The key turns in the lock. The grille is open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The grille is locked. You can try picking the lock; the iron will yield only to a suitable tool or heavy blows."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You take the relic from the quieted wound. Wear it to feel its strength. If you had no room in your belongings, the find was left at your feet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count: You raised your hand against what belongs to me.\nAnd came here again, as though you still had the right to ask for anything?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count: Branded one. You came to my house yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count: You entered my domain. Defend yourself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The Count: The time to ask for a place at court has passed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald: Baring your teeth at me?\nAbout time we found out what they're really worth!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald: Come on, swordsman. Show me why you're here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald: Come on! Show me what your words are worth!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rosine: I let you in. You knew where we lived.\nAnd you still did this?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rosine: Have you come to destroy my home?"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Rosine: Stay away from us!"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld: You broke your oath by your actions. Explanations will change nothing now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld: Raise your weapon. Your road onward goes through me."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld: The conversation is over."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A charred clasp is all that remains of the garrison banner. Names of the people who held the southern road are scratched on the back.\n\nThis is a human possession. The apostle's fiery shell did not belong to those whose names remain here."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The one the path leads to is nowhere to be seen among the bodies."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The wheel broke before dusk. The iron fastenings were left beneath the iron-bound chest; the grain was taken.\n\nAn order is tucked between the pages: \"Take the bent blades to Godo's forest forge. A young crossbow maker works with him. Follow the old cart tracks through the woods.\"\n\nTurns and crossings are marked in the margins."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We're leaving before the next dusk. The water is clean; those who follow may need the blanket more than we do.\n\nThe smith Godo repaired our broken blade. His young helper makes crossbow bolts. We wrote down the return route here: the old path, the stream crossing, then the charcoal burners' trail. It's a long walk, but there's a craftsman at the end of the road."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Mikhail, if you reach the camp first: we moved the wounded to the southwest tent. The creature came out of the northern tent and caught Pavel in the open. Keep behind the tent walls and leave through the gap in the eastern fence. We are leaving before dusk.\n\nLena."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The last prayer is crossed out.\n\nWe barred the main doors to keep strangers out. Now footsteps sound inside. Irina carried the remaining blankets through the vestry; I couldn't persuade her to return for the stone. The western wall is breached. Follow the living while there is still time."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The eastern passage is wide enough to carry him, but the scratches there are fresh. I left the iron crowbar by the broken support. We circled the stone pendant and approached the prop from below. The peg can be pulled out from that side.\n\nIf he wakes, first we'll try to reach the stairs, not the red face."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The paper charm retains a faint scent of herbs."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The flesh dissolves beneath your skin. The change has begun and will continue on its own. Find water, food and a place to rest."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The plate armor disappears into the swelling body. Stone-heavy bulk gives way to a glowing carapace."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Between the charred edges are a broken road, a ruined foundation and markings around a fissure. The creature from the hollow carried this route to another breach."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Where the figure vanished, a strange stone remains."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The trail of missing travelers leads into a forest hollow. A creature that hunts people hides here. Before descending, I should examine the approaches and leave a way to retreat."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The trail leads to a house beside an enormous tree. The information names a witch, Flora."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The figure's outlines come apart. Emptiness remains in its place, but the events around you do not stop. The Skull Knight appears between you and the closing darkness."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The forest forge is marked on your map."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "This information was not enough to establish the way to the forge. The trail is saved."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You chose a shelter beside the protective sign. It will weaken the Brand's call nearby, but creatures already here remain dangerous."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The previous sign's protection no longer holds. If you need a new shelter, examine another sign."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Clean cloth for dressings must be boiled. A waterskin is best sewn before a long journey. Drinking water, a sleeping place and a clear exit matter more than a comfortable room.\n\nA small sign of stone and bone helps restrain the nighttime call, but does not drive away a creature already standing at the door."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The edges of the pages are curled and blackened, crumbling at a touch. A few surviving lines can still be read between the charred edges: fragments of phrases without beginning or end. The fire took the rest completely. Nothing can bring it back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora compares the joined worlds to roots grown together across a wound. A quiet place can shelter a traveler; one refuge cannot heal the whole world.\n\nTraces of smoke remain in the margins. Most of the research lay beyond the torn pages."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We left the cart on the old path. The face is caught in the roots, just as he said. While the creature circled the trunk, I waited behind the thick roots and didn't move.\n\nWe'll return by the old western path. If only one of us reaches the cart, leave the other's name on the cord."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Dry the herbs separately. Boil clean cloth for wounds. Mend old sleeves before the next journey. Keep both passages around the spirit tree clear.\n\nA refuge remains a refuge because someone cares for it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I marked the broad gallery to the east. Beneath it, a narrow tunnel skirts the rock and joins the gallery twice. In the western hall we heard the pendant before we saw what followed its sound. The bends hid us from its eyes.\n\nThere is a passage with a support near the stairs, but the peg faces deeper into the cave. If we make it, I'll leave another mark by the broken prop."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Water was stored in the eastern room, blankets and dressings in the vestry. An early entry mentions a traveler with a repaired sword and bolts: \"Godo's forge is still working in the forest. The old man and his young helper take usable metal in payment.\" He drew the road on the back.\n\nLater, instead of food portions, they began counting hours beside the red stone. The last volunteer wrote: \"This was meant to be a refuge.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "We called the stone a miracle because we needed a miracle. We moved it behind the altar and stopped opening the door to strangers. When the whispering began, we decided we had been answered.\n\nThe handprints on the altar were not left during prayer."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "If the chapel is lost, leave through the breach in the western wall. An old rut farther into the forest leads to a great oak with tangled roots. Travelers spoke of another stone face. I have not seen it myself."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The extraction order is crossed out.\n\nThree of us described the same red face after spending the night here. When we moved the sample, scratching began behind the new tent. Pavel is wounded: the creature caught him when he stepped into the open. Cancel sample collection. Send transport for the wounded. We are leaving the equipment."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You write down again what you kept in memory."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A heavy seal left by the Count. Worn, it helps strike beings from beyond the boundary. Its power is not directed against every living body."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A sinewy knot sharpens the sense of what moves in darkness. With it, the night road is easier to make out."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A thin veil retains a trace of the strange valley. Worn, it helps evade a blow, but promises no escape from every attack."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The shard belongs to the apostle itself. Worn, it helps endure heat, but does not protect against smoke or make fire safe.\n\nIt cannot be confused with the charred clasps of the garrison's people."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The path ends abruptly, as though the world itself decided where to stop it. The space ahead resembles neither forest nor cave nor anything familiar: light comes from nowhere and everywhere at once, casting no shadows.\n\nFive figures stand in a semicircle. None steps forward. They wait, as though approaching were your decision.\n\nA heavy pulse beats in your palm, though the stone is no longer there.\n\nVoid: \"The call was heard. You have reached the place where you may give your answer.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Void: You turned your actions against those whose answer you still awaited.\n\nThe five voices fall silent. At the beginning of the path, the closed passage tears open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Slan: So that is how you chose to express your desire. Very well. We shall see.\n\nThe five voices fall silent. At the beginning of the path, the closed passage tears open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Ubik: Now we'll see whether you can reach the road back.\n\nThe five voices fall silent. At the beginning of the path, the closed passage tears open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "He turns his whole body toward you, slowly, like everything he does. He speaks no further word.\n\nThe five voices fall silent. At the beginning of the path, the closed passage tears open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Femto: Not enough.\n\nThe five voices fall silent. At the beginning of the path, the closed passage tears open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The five voices fall silent. At the beginning of the path, the closed passage tears open."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The fifth figure comes apart. The pressure vanishes. Beyond the dead field, the living world can be felt again; the way back is open at the beginning of the path."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The living tissue has closed. The passage does not respond."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You wrench free of the passage. Pain burns through your skin. Before the darkness can close again, a rider in a skull-shaped helmet appears between you and it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The thread has broken. You stand beneath the sky of your former world. No one emerged from the passage behind you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Flora does not offer you the bundle. Speak to her about the armor first."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The charm has already served its purpose."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "There is no exit ahead. The torn passage remains where you entered this field."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You stand beneath familiar skies again. Something foreign stirs within. What you accepted did not stay behind the threshold."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You returned human. But silence brings no peace: something of what you endured has stayed with you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The names recur on execution notices. Shoes and cloaks were sorted before sentencing, as though their owner had already ceased to be a person. One entry was crossed out and replaced with \"sent below.\"\n\nBehind every neat column was a person they had already decided was a thing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The first pages concern boiled linen and ordinary wounds. Then sketches appear of a second mouth growing from a servant's chest.\n\nThe author stopped calling it a disease. Pieces of the master's flesh implanted another life in the victim. Familiar treatments did not restore the person."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The ribbon lay beside sewing and a book kept free of dust. A note calls the room Theresia's and forbids the servants to disturb it.\n\nThe same ruler who signed the prison lists protected this little island of ordinary life. It does not say where his daughter is now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The pact is broken. The changed flesh remains with you."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The bond with your master has broken. Your body remains as it was."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Accept the gift? Your body will change immediately and forever. The master and his followers will leave you and your companions alone while you honor the pact. An attack from your side will break it."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "An alien power reshapes your flesh."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The lists separate soldiers, prisoners and those taken to the commander. The first pages record boot sizes and rations. Later notes describe distorted guards wearing the same uniforms.\n\nAnother life of the camp shows through the familiar military ledger."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "I hid this before roll call. The cage doors are tied, not locked with iron keys. Untie them from either side and pass through. The route through the quarry is longer, but open.\n\nAt the bottom, a short word has been added beside one name: \"escaped.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wyald ordered the plundered supplies counted and a space cleared for fighting. Wooden barriers were dragged to the edges. Between the lines about spoils and people, one demand recurs: no one leaves without his permission.\n\nThe last sheet speaks of a fractured world. The crossing changed the commander's former fate. The one living in this camp is the man himself, not his reflection."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "They called the winged things fairies because the flowers were beautiful. I followed a trail of abandoned shoes, past the games, toward the silk.\n\nIn the quiet shells, no hope remained. In the moving ones was something already changed. I cannot bring them back. The western ravine offers a way around the grove to the enormous roots."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The ribbon was tied to a branch as a marker for a game. Farther on, the same knot is caught in a split shell. The flowers kept growing after the games stopped.\n\nSometimes all a person leaves is a thing easily walked past."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Find a place to rest before continuing along the known roads."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You lost sight of him in the smoke. Whether he lives or is dead is unknown. An empty place is not a dead body."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld is dead. But the wounds bound to him did not disappear with him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld survived. The remaining trail leads to his fortress. You can recover your strength before continuing."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld survived and vanished in the smoke. Where he went after the battle remains to be discovered."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Smoke stings your eyes before you realize you are outside. The trees part, and there it is: the great tree, black against the flames. Where windows once stood are only orange hollows, with something moving within them: heat, perhaps, or what remains of the roof.\n\nYou stood by that hearth. Spoke with its mistress and came to know this house. Now it burns, and there is nowhere left to go but forward.\n\nThe closed breaches gave the land a respite, no more. Darkness still seeps into a world that had not recovered from the Cataclysm. You cannot yet begin to imagine how much remains to be done to mend even a little of these wounds.\n\nToday, you stayed alive. For now, that is enough.\n\n<context_val:flora_next>"
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A broken throwing-knife hilt lies among torn equipment. A hand has worn the wood smooth; a dark thread remains at the broken end.\n\nYou recognize it. Judeau noticed others' needs before they asked. Now there is nothing left to ask him."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A broken throwing-knife hilt lies among torn equipment. A hand has worn the wood smooth; a dark thread remains at the broken end.\n\nThe name \"Judeau\" means nothing to you yet. A person died here; you do not yet know his life."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "You have already examined this place. What you learned is saved."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A large fighter's body remains beside a narrow passage. Nearby lies a heavy clasp torn from shattered armor. Fresh scratches cross old hammer marks.\n\nPippin rarely wasted words. Beside him, you seldom needed to ask whether he would cover your back."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A large fighter's body remains beside a narrow passage. Nearby lies a heavy clasp torn from shattered armor. Fresh scratches cross old hammer marks.\n\nThe name \"Pippin\" means nothing to you yet. A person died here; you do not yet know his life."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A broken fragment of scabbard lies beside the body. The former owner's fingers polished the leather; ash is caught in a split seam.\n\nYou remember his voice, his irritation, his arguments. Memory brings back a living person, not convenient words about a fallen comrade."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A broken fragment of scabbard lies beside the body. The former owner's fingers polished the leather; ash is caught in a split seam.\n\nThe name \"Corkus\" means nothing to you yet. A person died here; you do not yet know his life."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Needles and scraps from a crushed sewing kit are scattered beneath a dented breastplate. Small, neat repairs survived among rough tears.\n\nGaston spoke of life after the war. You recognize his sewing kit and remember how earnestly he made those plans."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Needles and scraps from a crushed sewing kit are scattered beneath a dented breastplate. Small, neat repairs survived among rough tears.\n\nThe sewing kit does not explain who the dead man was. But someone treasured these needles and found time for careful work."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Alien limbs close around you. The ground gives way beneath your feet."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The outer defense is failing. Get away from the entrance. Now."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Wood cracks outside. Demons move between the trunks through the smoke."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The smoke thickens. Burning branches snap off above the house."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A motionless figure stands among the moving bodies ahead. The other creatures seem to leave a space clear around it.\n\n\"Griffith!\"\n\nThe figure turns its head."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A motionless figure stands among the moving bodies ahead. The other creatures seem to leave a space clear around it.\n\n\"Are you controlling them?\"\n\nThere is no answer. But now you feel that your approach has been noticed."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A heavy impact sounds beyond the outer boundary. An enormous figure appears between the trees.\n\nZodd: \"Show me how far you've come, swordsman.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A heavy impact sounds beyond the outer boundary. An enormous figure appears between the trees.\n\nZodd: \"Step aside if you want to live.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld stops at the outer boundary. \"Step away from the house.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Zodd: \"So you're staying.\""
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "Grunbeld: \"You chose to defend it. Then withstand the blow.\""
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "What do you remember of the Band?"
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Judeau always noticed when someone needed help. He taught me things without making me feel a fool."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "I found a trace of Judeau. I did not know him."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Then remember him doing that. You said he made things easier for others. His last moments do not take that away."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Then speak of what you found. Neither of us knew his life. We can at least leave room for it, instead of inventing one."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "I am afraid I will forget their voices."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "And I am here, alive."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "There is someone else I want to remember."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Enough for today. Thank you for listening."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Pippin hardly spoke. But if he stood behind you, you knew your back was covered."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "I found a trace of Pippin. I did not know him."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Some men spend their whole lives promising that. He did it. You have something worth remembering."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Corkus and I argued all the time. Now I catch myself wishing I could hear him grumble again."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "I found a trace of Corkus. I did not know him."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "You need not turn him into a saint to miss him. Remember the arguments too. That was a living man, not a statue."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Gaston wanted to leave the war and open a shop. I keep remembering how certain he sounded."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "I found a trace of Gaston. I did not know him."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "A shop, a roof, work of his own. I understand that wish. Do not let the way he died swallow the life he wanted."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Tell the boy, if you can. He knew them. Say one thing you remember, then another. You do not have to carry every voice alone."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "I want to remember someone else."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Thank you. I need some time."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Yes. That is what we have to work with. Eat, mend what can be mended, and decide how to live tomorrow. You owe the dead more than another body."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "First, get help from Rickert"
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Speak to Rickert at the forest forge about replacing your lost left hand. He can build a prosthetic arm cannon if you bring the materials; ask him what is needed and deliver them to him. You may pursue the hunts with your own equipment, but restoring your grip will make the road much easier. Install the finished device from your inventory."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "The Skull Knight waits outside the door. He wanted to speak with you before leaving. If you need a replacement hand, speak to Rickert first. His help is listed in your missions."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "The Skull Knight waits nearby. He wanted to speak with you before leaving. If you need a replacement hand, speak to Rickert first. His help is listed in your missions."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Reach the marked ashen breach and defeat its guardian. Then examine the exposed wound in the earth to close it. Examine the quieted mark afterward to collect what remains. Closing this passage reveals the next known hunts in your mission list."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Reach the Count's residence and confront him below the execution hall. After defeating him, examine the exposed breach in the dungeon, then examine the sealed mark to take the relic. The prisoner and written evidence are optional help; neither is required to close the breach."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Reach the Black Dogs' camp and confront Wyald in its final clearing. After defeating him, examine the exposed breach in the northern part of that clearing. Then examine the sealed mark to collect the relic. No journal or particular spoken challenge is required."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Reach the misty valley and confront Rosine among the great roots. After defeating her, examine the exposed wound at her nest to close the passage. Then examine the sealed mark to collect the relic. You can leave cocoons behind; clearing every creature is not required."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Before hunting, consider asking Rickert at the forge for a replacement hand if you need one. Find and defeat the predator in the marked hollow. After the fight, examine the surviving trail in the lair; it gives the next mission even without a journal or the scrap of paper."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Reach the Black Dogs' camp and confront Wyald in its final clearing. After defeating him, examine the exposed breach in the northern part of that clearing to close it. Then examine the sealed mark to collect the relic."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Should I tell Rickert what I found?"
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "I found other traces too."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Then tell me. I did not know their voices, but I can listen. Say one thing you remember, then another."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Reach the marked stronghold and follow the passage to the crucible. Deal with its keeper if he is still alive. Once the wound is exposed, examine the breach north of the crucible to close it, then examine the sealed mark to recover the relic."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How have you been?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I keep finding work for my hands. It is quieter here than it was with the Band of the Hawk. I miss their voices."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is always something to mend. When I stop, I start thinking about the Band of the Hawk. I miss the people, even the noise around the campfire."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The Band of the Hawk? Will you tell me about it?"
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "How have you been holding up?"
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "Supplies and a bundle of papers show beneath the broken wagon. You could approach the wreckage and examine what is still there."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "A field log is pinned to the table in the northwestern tent. Its pages are still legible; you could examine the abandoned equipment beside it."
msgstr ""

#. Owner playtest fixes 2026-10-24
msgid "An old list of travelers and donated supplies survives near the southern entrance. Some writing remains beneath the later scratches."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A note in the margin reads: \"If we get out, find the smith Godo. He and his young helper repaired our fittings and crossbow. The route to his forest forge is marked on the back.\" A list of turns and a stream crossing follows."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "The extraction order is crossed out.\n\nThree of us described the same red face after spending the night here. When we moved the sample, scratching began behind the new tent. Pavel is wounded: the creature caught him when he stepped into the open. Cancel sample collection. Send transport for the wounded. We are leaving the equipment.\n\nA note in the margin reads: \"If we get out, find the smith Godo. He and his young helper repaired our fittings and crossbow. The route to his forest forge is marked on the back.\" A list of turns and a stream crossing follows."
msgstr ""

#. English base source; approved Russian manuscript 2026-10-24
msgid "A note in the margin reads: \"If we get out, find the smith Godo. He and his young helper repaired our fittings and crossbow. The route to his forest forge is marked on the back.\" A list of turns and a stream crossing follows.\n\n"
msgstr ""
